    "https://jobs.snhu.edu/en/jobs/r0014809/learning-resources-vendor-associate/": {
      "title": "Learning Resources Vendor Associate",
      "description": "Learning Resources Vendor Associate,  | SNHU Careers Skip to main content Who We Are Who We Are Culture Benefits Equity, Diversity & Inclusion Military Career Areas Career Areas Online Teaching Jobs Academics & Teaching Business Operations & Technology Campus Staff Customer Service & Student Support Human Resources & Strategy Marketing & Communications Student Jobs Working at SNHU Working at SNHU Flexible Work Training & Development How We Hire 0 My Saved Jobs Search Jobs Academics Learning Resources Vendor Associate Full time October 13, 2026 Remote Description Southern New Hampshire University is a team of innovators. World changers. Individuals who believe in progress with purpose. Since 1932, our people-centered strategy has defined us — and helped us grow a team that now serves over 180,000 learners worldwide. Our mission to transform lives is made possible by talented people who bring diverse industry experience, backgrounds and skills to the university. And today, we're ready to expand our reach. All we need is you. Make an impact — from near or far At SNHU, you'll have the option to work remotely in the following states: Alabama, Arizona, Arkansas, Delaware, Florida, Georgia, Hawaii, Idaho, Indiana, Iowa, Kansas, Kentucky, Louisiana, Maine, Maryland, Massachusetts, Michigan, Mississippi, Missouri, Nebraska, New Hampshire, New Mexico, North Carolina, North Dakota, Ohio, Oklahoma, South Carolina, South Dakota, Tennessee, Texas, Utah, Vermont, Virginia, West Virginia, Wisconsin and Wyoming. We ask that our remote employees have access to a reliable internet connection and a dedicated, properly equipped workspace that is free of distractions. Employees must reside in, and work from, one of the above approved states. The opportunity As the Learning Resources Vendor Associate you will support and manage third-party and digital learning resources that support academic programs. What you'll do: You will be an important liaison between faculty, internal academic partners, vendors, and the online bookstore. You'll ensure learning resources are accurate, accessible, scalable, cost-effective, and aligned with curriculum and institutional goals. You will blend operational execution, vendor relationship management, data analysis, and collaboration to enhance the student and faculty experience across online learning environments. You'll report to the Director of Learning Resources. This is a remote position. What we're looking for: Years of experience: One year of experience for the learning resource bookstore operations and service support team; three years' experience for learning resource vendor management and program development team. Degree(s): Bachelor's degree in education, instructional design, educational technology, or related field. Equivalent of experience in lieu of degree acceptable: Yes Professional Certification(s): N/A Project management skills with the ability to manage multiple priorities simultaneously. The ability to collaborate across departments and with external partners. Proficiency with Microsoft Office and familiarity with learning technologies and learning management systems. Preferred Qualifications: Experience working with higher education learning management systems and digital coursework platforms. Knowledge of accessibility standards (e.g., ADA, WCAG) and digital equity principles. Experience analyzing adoption, usage, or engagement data to inform decision-making. Exposure to digital transformation projects, catalog optimization, or large-scale academic resource projects. #LI-Remote We believe real innovation comes from inclusion - where different experiences, perspectives and talents are celebrated. So if you're wondering whether SNHU is right for you, take the leap and apply. You might be just the person we're looking for. If you have a disability and require a reasonable accommodation to fully engage in any part of the application or hiring process, please complete the Accommodation Request form or contact us at 603-626-9447. A member from the Employee Accommodation Support Center will be in contact with you within two business days to discuss your request. Compensation The annual pay range for this position is $49,750.00 - $79,615.00. Actual offer will be based on skills, qualifications, experience and internal equity, in addition to relevant business considerations. We expect this position to be hired in the following target hiring range $54,974.00 - $74,376.00. Exceptional benefits (because you’re exceptional) You’re the whole package. Your benefits should be, too. As a full-time employee at SNHU, you’ll get: High-quality, low-deductible medical insurance Low to no-cost dental and vision plans 5 weeks of paid time off (plus almost a dozen paid holidays) Employer-funded retirement Free tuition program Parental leave Mental health and wellbeing resources Apply Now Save Saved Share Share Related Jobs Employer Relations Partner I Save Saved Student Services Remote IAM Engineer Save Saved Information Technology Remote Senior Financial Analyst Strategic Initiatives and Technology Advancements Save Saved Finance Remote See all jobs Expect the unexpected As a university, it’s no surprise we employ many talented academics. What you may not know is that SNHU isn’t solely made up of folks with higher ed experience. Not even close. Where will your talent take you? See all teams Academics & Teaching Business Operations & Technology Campus Staff Customer Service & Student Support Human Resources & Strategy Marketing & Communications Student Jobs Don't see the job you're looking for? Connect with us anyway! We post new jobs frequently, and joining our talent community is a great way to be notified when we do. Join talent community Sitemap Cookies Corporate site Need an Accommodation? © SNHU 2026, all rights reserved. Thank you, your preferences have been updated. Manage Preferences Accept All Essential Only"
