    "https://jobs.snhu.edu/en/jobs/r0014758/vice-president-of-development-alumni-and-community-engagement/": {
      "title": "Student - Jayme's Fund for Social Justice Development and Communications Assistant (Work-Study Only)",
      "description": "Vice President of Development, Alumni, and Community Engagement,  | SNHU Careers Skip to main content Who We Are Who We Are Culture Benefits Equity, Diversity & Inclusion Military Career Areas Career Areas Online Teaching Jobs Academics & Teaching Business Operations & Technology Campus Staff Customer Service & Student Support Human Resources & Strategy Marketing & Communications Student Jobs Working at SNHU Working at SNHU Flexible Work Training & Development How We Hire 0 My Saved Jobs Search Jobs Administrative Vice President of Development, Alumni, and Community Engagement Full time October 13, 2026 Hybrid Description Southern New Hampshire University is a team of innovators. World changers. Individuals who believe in progress with purpose. Since 1932, our people-centered strategy has defined us — and helped us grow a team that now serves over 180,000 learners worldwide. Our mission to transform lives is made possible by talented people who bring diverse industry experience, backgrounds and skills to the university. And today, we're ready to expand our reach. All we need is you. This position will be partially based in the following office location: Manchester, NH For hybrid roles, employees must be able to commute to Manchester, NH on a regular basis. The opportunity As the Vice President of Development, Alumni, and Community engagement, you will provide strategic leadership for philanthropic giving, alumni engagement, and community engagement at Southern New Hampshire University, unifying these functions into a single strategy that advances the university's mission and growth. For all three areas, you will build and sustain authentic, long-term relationships with donors, alumni, community leaders, board members, and university partners, serving as a compelling ambassador for the institution. As a key member of the Office of External Affairs and Communications leadership team, you will bring bold, mission-driven leadership to each of these areas. Reporting to the Executive Vice President and Chief External Affairs and Communications Officer, you will lead a team of advancement and alumni and community engagement professionals and model a culture of excellence, collaboration, accountability, and continuous development. In philanthropic giving, you are the primary architect of a comprehensive, multi-year development strategy that expands revenue through major gifts, planned giving, annual giving, corporate and foundation relations, and campaign initiatives. In alumni engagement, you build an active, invested network of alumni who advance the institution's mission and reputation. In community engagement, you provide leadership to strengthen and expand community partnerships and promote service-learning opportunities, and ensure SNHU is a deeply embedded and trusted partner in the Manchester community and beyond. #LI-Remote What you'll do: You will oversee efforts to strengthen the university's capacity to leverage the passion, expertise, and generosity of our extensive network of alumni, donors, foundation and community partners, and volunteers. The VP secures external support for SNHU's highest priorities and advances the institution's vision of accessible, affordable, and transformative education. You will integrate strategic planning, data-informed decision-making, and inclusive practices to grow philanthropic capacity while deepening the university's ties to the communities it serves. Strategic Planning & Prioritization : You will develop a unifying strategy across philanthropy, alumni engagement, and community engagement that reflects SNHU's mission. You will establish a clear vision, set measurable goals, and ensure institutional resources and energy are aligned with the university's highest priorities. You will serve as a strategic advisor to senior leadership on all matters of institutional advancement. Development and Annual Giving: You will lead the development team to identify, cultivate, and secure philanthropic support for SNHU's institutional priorities. You will build and continuously refine a comprehensive fundraising strategy encompassing annual giving, major gifts, and planned giving. You will distribute donor relationships and fundraising responsibility across the team in a way that maximizes reach, deepens portfolio depth, and builds institutional resilience. You will set clear performance expectations and ensure the team has the tools, data, and support to succeed. Donor Relations : You will provide strategic direction for donor relations, ensuring existing and prospective donors experience exceptional stewardship, meaningful recognition, and a genuine connection to SNHU's mission and impact. Alumni Engagement : You will oversee a robust and innovative alumni engagement program that cultivates meaningful, lifelong relationships with alumni. Lead the development of programs and events that promote engagement and give alumni purposeful and varied ways to invest in SNHU's success, as donors, volunteers, advocates and community leaders. Community Engagement and Service: You will strengthen and expand community giving and partnerships, promote service-learning opportunities, and oversee community giving and programming that reflect SNHU's mission and values. You will ensure SNHU is a deeply embedded and trusted partner in the New Hampshire community and beyond, and champion the connection between SNHU's community work and its overarching mission. Advancement Services: You will oversee all advancement services functions, including database management, gift processing, prospect research, and reporting. You will champion a data-informed culture within the team, ensuring accurate and actionable data is available to support donor strategy, decision-making, and accountability. You will leverage advancement data to identify opportunities, track progress against goals, and communicate impact to internal and external stakeholders. Grant Management and Capacity Building : You will build and institutionalize sustainable grant management capacity, including clear processes, compliance infrastructure, and institutional policy to reduce single point of failure risk and strengthen the university's ability to pursue and steward external grant funding effectively. Stakeholder Collaboration : You will serve as a trusted connector and strategic liaison between the advancement team and university leadership and other institutional partners. You will strengthen the university's capacity to engage alumni, donors, volunteers, and community partners cohesively and in support of student success. You will model a collaborative, cross-functional leadership approach that breaks down silos and amplifies institutional impact. Team Leadership & Culture : You will build, inspire, and unify a diverse advancement division spanning philanthropy, alumni engagement, and community programs. You will set clear expectations for accountability, collaboration, and professional excellence. You will create structures and practices that promote team cohesion, cross-functional knowledge, sharing, and staff development. You will cultivate a division culture that is mission-centered, inclusive and resilient, one in which every team member understands how their work connects to SNHU's broader purpose and the learners it serves. What we're looking for: 10+ years of progressive experience in fundraising, advancement, development or related fields, including success building and scaling fundraising programs and teams. Bachelor's degree in nonprofit management, higher education administration, business, public administration, or a related field Proven track record of closing significant philanthropic gifts and cultivating long-term donor relationships that result in sustained philanthropic investment. Demonstrated experience leading and developing diverse, multi-functional teams with a track record of building collaborative, accountable, and high-performing team cultures. Exceptional communication skills — written, verbal, and presentational — with the ability to inspire and engage donors, community leaders, board members, and institutional partners. Strong strategic planning and organizational acumen, with the ability to set vision, prioritize resources, and translate strategy into measurable outcomes. Curious mindset, with a genuine understanding of and appreciation for service and community work. Demonstrated systems thinking orientation, with the ability to understand how data, technology, and operational infrastructure connect to and enable advancement strategy. Demonstrated ability to unify a broad, diverse team around a shared strategy spanning philanthropy, alumni engagement, and community work. Demonstrated commitment and alignment with SNHU's mission of accessible, affordable, and transformative education. Target Hiring Range: We expect this position to be hired within the target hiring range of $225,000–$275,000 . Actual offer will be based on skills, qualifications, experience and internal equity, in addition to relevant business considerations. We believe real innovation comes from inclusion - where different experiences, perspectives and talents are celebrated. So if you're wondering whether SNHU is right for you, take the leap and apply. You might be just the person we're looking for. If you have a disability and require a reasonable accommodation to fully engage in any part of the application or hiring process, please complete the Accommodation Request form or contact us at 603-626-9447. A member from the Employee Accommodation Support Center will be in contact with you within two business days to discuss your request. Compensation The annual pay range for this position is $200,000.00 - $400,000.00. Actual offer will be based on skills, qualifications, experience and internal equity, in addition to relevant business considerations. Exceptional benefits (because you’re exceptional) You’re the whole package. Your benefits should be, too. As a full-time employee at SNHU, you’ll get: High-quality, low-deductible medical insurance Low to no-cost dental and vision plans 5 weeks of paid time off (plus almost a dozen paid holidays) Employer-funded retirement Free tuition program Parental leave Mental health and wellbeing resources Apply Now Save Saved Share Share Related Jobs Senior Financial Analyst Strategic Initiatives and Technology Advancements Save Saved Finance Remote Employer Relations Partner I Save Saved Student Services Remote Student - Jayme's Fund for Social Justice Development and Communications Assistant (Work-Study Only) Save Saved Student Jobs On-Site (New Hampshire) See all jobs Expect the unexpected As a university, it’s no surprise we employ many talented academics. What you may not know is that SNHU isn’t solely made up of folks with higher ed experience. Not even close. Where will your talent take you? See all teams Academics & Teaching Business Operations & Technology Campus Staff Customer Service & Student Support Human Resources & Strategy Marketing & Communications Student Jobs Don't see the job you're looking for? Connect with us anyway! We post new jobs frequently, and joining our talent community is a great way to be notified when we do. Join talent community Sitemap Cookies Corporate site Need an Accommodation? © SNHU 2026, all rights reserved. Thank you, your preferences have been updated. Manage Preferences Accept All Essential Only"
    },
    "https://jobs.snhu.edu/en/jobs/r0014854/clinical-faculty-health-sciences/": {
      "title": "Learning Resources Vendor Associate",
      "description": "Clinical Faculty, Health Sciences,  | SNHU Careers Skip to main content Who We Are Who We Are Culture Benefits Equity, Diversity & Inclusion Military Career Areas Career Areas Online Teaching Jobs Academics & Teaching Business Operations & Technology Campus Staff Customer Service & Student Support Human Resources & Strategy Marketing & Communications Student Jobs Working at SNHU Working at SNHU Flexible Work Training & Development How We Hire 0 My Saved Jobs Search Jobs Academics Clinical Faculty, Health Sciences Full time October 13, 2026 Remote Description Southern New Hampshire University is a team of innovators. World changers. Individuals who believe in progress with purpose. Since 1932, our people-centered strategy has defined us — and helped us grow a team that now serves over 180,000 learners worldwide. Our mission to transform lives is made possible by talented people who bring diverse industry experience, backgrounds and skills to the university. And today, we're ready to expand our reach. All we need is you. Make an impact — from near or far At SNHU, you'll have the option to work remotely in the following states: Alabama, Arizona, Arkansas, Delaware, Florida, Georgia, Hawaii, Idaho, Indiana, Iowa, Kansas, Kentucky, Louisiana, Maine, Maryland, Massachusetts, Michigan, Mississippi, Missouri, Nebraska, New Hampshire, New Mexico, North Carolina, North Dakota, Ohio, Oklahoma, South Carolina, South Dakota, Tennessee, Texas, Utah, Vermont, Virginia, West Virginia, Wisconsin and Wyoming. We ask that our remote employees have access to a reliable internet connection and a dedicated, properly equipped workspace that is free of distractions. Employees must reside in, and work from, one of the above approved states. The opportunity TSouthern New Hampshire University is a team of innovators. World changers. Individuals who believe in progress with purpose. Since 1932, our people-centered strategy has defined us — and helped us grow a team that now serves over 180,000 learners worldwide. Our mission to transform lives is made possible by talented people who bring diverse industry experience, backgrounds and skills to the university. And today, we're ready to expand our reach. All we need is you. Make an impact — from near or far At SNHU, you'll have the option to work remotely in the following states: Alabama, Arizona, Arkansas, Delaware, Florida, Georgia, Hawaii, Idaho, Indiana, Iowa, Kansas, Kentucky, Louisiana, Maine, Maryland, Massachusetts, Michigan, Mississippi, Missouri, Nebraska, New Hampshire, New Mexico, North Carolina, North Dakota, Ohio, Oklahoma, South Carolina, South Dakota, Tennessee, Texas, Utah, Vermont, Virginia, West Virginia, Wisconsin and Wyoming. We ask that our remote employees have access to a reliable internet connection and a dedicated, properly equipped workspace that is free of distractions. Employees must reside in, and work from, one of the above approved states. The opportunity As a Clinical Faculty member in the Health Sciences Program, your role is to support specified online programs within Global Campus through teaching, student support, subject-matter-expertise, mentoring of adjunct faculty and engagement in administrative activities in service of the institution. You'll teach standardized, pre-developed online courses, in an 8-week undergraduate term. In addition to teaching, you'll serve in varied academic administrative capacities to help ensure that Global Campus programs, courses, and instruction are high quality and meet the institutional promise to students. You will report to the Program Director, Health Sciences. We are a remote friendly work environment. #LI-Remote What you'll do: Teach 36 credit hours (two courses per term) annually Follow all instructional principles and strategies that engage students in learning, when serving as a course instructor while following the pre-determined course design and textbook materials Provide meaningful feedback to students, academic advisors and team lead following faculty expectations and requirements. Follow the Instructional Practices Rubric and faculty performance standards Participate in program specific events including graduation activities, academic residencies, and professional development activities Collaborate with enrollment and student advisors to support program growth and student persistence Provide exceptional student service in every interaction, which includes never giving up on a student who is putting forth the effort to achieve their goals Participate in any scholarly and professional activities required to contribute to one's academic discipline, maintain licensure and compliance with regulatory and accrediting agencies that have jurisdiction over the faculty's respective program What we're looking for: Doctoral Degree in Health Science or a closely related field, from a regionally accredited institution Minimum of 3 years of experience practicing in the respective field Online teaching experience We believe real innovation comes from inclusion - where different experiences, perspectives and talents are celebrated. So if you're wondering whether SNHU is right for you, take the leap and apply. You might be just the person we're looking for. If you have a disability and require a reasonable accommodation to fully engage in any part of the application or hiring process, please complete the Accommodation Request form or contact us at 603-626-9447. A member from the Employee Accommodation Support Center will be in contact with you within two business days to discuss your request. Compensation The annual pay range for this position is $72,851.00 - $116,584.00. Actual offer will be based on skills, qualifications, experience and internal equity, in addition to relevant business considerations. We expect this position to be hired in the following target hiring range $80,500.00 - $108,911.00. Exceptional benefits (because you’re exceptional) You’re the whole package. Your benefits should be, too. As a full-time employee at SNHU, you’ll get: High-quality, low-deductible medical insurance Low to no-cost dental and vision plans 5 weeks of paid time off (plus almost a dozen paid holidays) Employer-funded retirement Free tuition program Parental leave Mental health and wellbeing resources Apply Now Save Saved Share Share Related Jobs Learning Resources Vendor Associate Save Saved Academics Remote Senior Financial Analyst Strategic Initiatives and Technology Advancements Save Saved Finance Remote Modern Workplace Engineering Manager Save Saved Information Technology Remote See all jobs Expect the unexpected As a university, it’s no surprise we employ many talented academics. What you may not know is that SNHU isn’t solely made up of folks with higher ed experience. Not even close. Where will your talent take you? See all teams Academics & Teaching Business Operations & Technology Campus Staff Customer Service & Student Support Human Resources & Strategy Marketing & Communications Student Jobs Don't see the job you're looking for? Connect with us anyway! We post new jobs frequently, and joining our talent community is a great way to be notified when we do. Join talent community Sitemap Cookies Corporate site Need an Accommodation? © SNHU 2026, all rights reserved. Thank you, your preferences have been updated. Manage Preferences Accept All Essential Only"
