    "https://jobs.snhu.edu/en/jobs/r0014766/modern-workplace-engineering-manager/": {
      "title": "Learning Resources Vendor Associate",
      "description": "Modern Workplace Engineering Manager,  | SNHU Careers Skip to main content Who We Are Who We Are Culture Benefits Equity, Diversity & Inclusion Military Career Areas Career Areas Online Teaching Jobs Academics & Teaching Business Operations & Technology Campus Staff Customer Service & Student Support Human Resources & Strategy Marketing & Communications Student Jobs Working at SNHU Working at SNHU Flexible Work Training & Development How We Hire 0 My Saved Jobs Search Jobs Information Technology Modern Workplace Engineering Manager Full time October 13, 2026 Remote Description Southern New Hampshire University is a team of innovators. World changers. Individuals who believe in progress with purpose. Since 1932, our people-centered strategy has defined us — and helped us grow a team that now serves over 180,000 learners worldwide. Our mission to transform lives is made possible by talented people who bring diverse industry experience, backgrounds and skills to the university. And today, we're ready to expand our reach. All we need is you. Make an impact — from near or far At SNHU, you'll have the option to work remotely in the following states: Alabama, Arizona, Arkansas, Delaware, Florida, Georgia, Hawaii, Idaho, Indiana, Iowa, Kansas, Kentucky, Louisiana, Maine, Maryland, Massachusetts, Michigan, Mississippi, Missouri, Nebraska, New Hampshire, New Mexico, North Carolina, North Dakota, Ohio, Oklahoma, South Carolina, South Dakota, Tennessee, Texas, Utah, Vermont, Virginia, West Virginia, Wisconsin and Wyoming. We ask that our remote employees have access to a reliable internet connection and a dedicated, properly equipped workspace that is free of distractions. Employees must reside in, and work from, one of the above approved states. The opportunity The Modern Workplace Engineering Manager is a technical people-leader responsible for the daily operation, engineering, and continuous improvement of Southern New Hampshire University's Modern Workplace services. In this role, you will lead a team of engineers and administrators while remaining actively engaged in technical design, troubleshooting, implementation, and escalation support across Microsoft 365, endpoint management, collaboration, identity, automation, and related technologies. You will translate departmental strategy into technical execution ensuring work is properly prioritized and delivered. You will develop the capabilities of the team, and provide hands-on technical leadership for complex or high-impact initiatives. The position requires a strong balance of people leadership, operational discipline, and current technical expertise. You will report to the Director of Modern Workplace Engineering. #LI-Remote What you'll do: Lead, coach, and develop a team of Modern Workplace engineers and administrators. Provide hands-on technical leadership across Microsoft 365, endpoint management, collaboration, identity, security, automation, and device-management technologies. Serve as a senior escalation point for complex technical incidents, service disruptions, implementation challenges, and architectural decisions. Participate directly in technical discovery, solution design, configuration, testing, deployment, troubleshooting, and documentation when needed. Review technical designs, implementation plans, scripts, configurations, and operational procedures for quality, security, scalability, and supportability. Manage work intake, prioritization, resource assignment, execution, and follow-through across operational and project-based work. Translate departmental strategy and institutional requirements into technical roadmaps, delivery plans, and team assignments. Establish clear technical standards, engineering practices, documentation requirements, and accountability expectations. Conduct regular one-on-one meetings, performance discussions, technical coaching, and professional-development planning. Identify skill gaps and create opportunities for cross-training, knowledge sharing, mentoring, and technical growth. Partner with the Director on platform strategy, architecture, workforce planning, budgeting, vendor management, and service improvement. Coordinate technical delivery across Microsoft 365, Intune, Windows, macOS, MECM, Autopilot, Teams, SharePoint, OneDrive, Entra ID, Power Platform, Copilot, and related technologies. Work with Information Security, Infrastructure, Enterprise Applications, Service Management, and other ITS teams to design and deliver secure, reliable solutions. Support incident, problem, change, request, release, and configuration-management practices. Evaluate emerging technologies and recommend improvements to the Modern Workplace environment. Develop automation and encourage the use of scripting, standardization, and repeatable engineering practices. Monitor service performance, technical debt, workload distribution, platform health, and delivery outcomes. Communicate technical risks, dependencies, status, resource needs, and recommendations to leadership and stakeholders. Represent Modern Workplace Engineering in technical reviews, governance forums, project meetings, and operational discussions. Other responsibilities as assigned What we're looking for: Seven or more years of progressive experience in Microsoft 365, endpoint engineering, infrastructure, systems administration, Modern Workplace technologies, or a related technical field. Three or more years of formal people-management, supervisory, technical-leadership, or team-leadership experience. Bachelor's degree or equivalent years of experience in lieu of degree acceptable Strong hands-on experience with Microsoft 365 administration and at least two major Modern Workplace disciplines, such as endpoint management, collaboration, identity, automation, messaging, or device engineering. Experience troubleshooting complex technical issues and guiding engineers through resolution. Experience designing, implementing, and supporting enterprise-scale technology solutions. Experience reviewing technical designs, scripts, configurations, implementation plans, and operational documentation. Demonstrated experience coaching technical employees, managing performance, and supporting career development. Experience managing competing operational priorities, escalations, projects, and technical resources. Working knowledge of IT service-management, security, governance, and change-management practices. Strong communication, decision-making, organizational, and stakeholder-management skills. We believe real innovation comes from inclusion - where different experiences, perspectives and talents are celebrated. So if you're wondering whether SNHU is right for you, take the leap and apply. You might be just the person we're looking for. If you have a disability and require a reasonable accommodation to fully engage in any part of the application or hiring process, please complete the Accommodation Request form or contact us at 603-626-9447. A member from the Employee Accommodation Support Center will be in contact with you within two business days to discuss your request. Compensation The annual pay range for this position is $96,954.00 - $155,153.00. Actual offer will be based on skills, qualifications, experience and internal equity, in addition to relevant business considerations. We expect this position to be hired in the following target hiring range $107,132.00 - $144,945.00. Exceptional benefits (because you’re exceptional) You’re the whole package. Your benefits should be, too. As a full-time employee at SNHU, you’ll get: High-quality, low-deductible medical insurance Low to no-cost dental and vision plans 5 weeks of paid time off (plus almost a dozen paid holidays) Employer-funded retirement Free tuition program Parental leave Mental health and wellbeing resources Apply Now Save Saved Share Share Related Jobs Senior Financial Analyst Strategic Initiatives and Technology Advancements Save Saved Finance Remote Learning Resources Vendor Associate Save Saved Academics Remote Employer Relations Partner I Save Saved Student Services Remote See all jobs Expect the unexpected As a university, it’s no surprise we employ many talented academics. What you may not know is that SNHU isn’t solely made up of folks with higher ed experience. Not even close. Where will your talent take you? See all teams Academics & Teaching Business Operations & Technology Campus Staff Customer Service & Student Support Human Resources & Strategy Marketing & Communications Student Jobs Don't see the job you're looking for? Connect with us anyway! We post new jobs frequently, and joining our talent community is a great way to be notified when we do. Join talent community Sitemap Cookies Corporate site Need an Accommodation? © SNHU 2026, all rights reserved. Thank you, your preferences have been updated. Manage Preferences Accept All Essential Only"
