    "https://jobs.snhu.edu/en/jobs/r0014839/administrative-coordinator/": {
      "title": "Administrative Coordinator",
      "description": "Administrative Coordinator,  | SNHU Careers Skip to main content Who We Are Who We Are Culture Benefits Equity, Diversity & Inclusion Military Career Areas Career Areas Online Teaching Jobs Academics & Teaching Business Operations & Technology Campus Staff Customer Service & Student Support Human Resources & Strategy Marketing & Communications Student Jobs Working at SNHU Working at SNHU Flexible Work Training & Development How We Hire 0 My Saved Jobs Search Jobs Administrative Administrative Coordinator Part time October 06, 2026 On-Site (New Hampshire) Description Southern New Hampshire University is a team of innovators. World changers. Individuals who believe in progress with purpose. Since 1932, our people-centered strategy has defined us — and helped us grow a team that now serves over 180,000 learners worldwide. Our mission to transform lives is made possible by talented people who bring diverse industry experience, backgrounds and skills to the university. And today, we're ready to expand our reach. All we need is you. This position is based in the following office location: New Hampshire The opportunity The Administrative Office Coordinator performs routine administrative responsibilities under close supervision. This role completes tasks using various office technologies, maintains schedules, coordinates meetings, assembles information, prepares routine reports, manuals, agendas, and correspondence, maintains necessary office supplies for supervisor/group supported, ensures various office equipment is properly installed and maintained, and interfaces with a variety of people, both internally and externally, in routine matters. Primary Duties and Responsibilities: Supports assigned group/supervisor performing routine administrative responsibilities. Completes a variety of tasks using various office technologies. Maintains schedules and coordinates meetings. Assembles information, prepares routine reports, manuals, agendas, and correspondence. Ensures necessary office supplies are always maintained. Makes sure various office equipment is properly installed and maintained. Works collaboratively with a variety of internal and external stakeholders. Attendance, punctuality, and reliability are essential functions of this role. Other duties and responsibilities as assigned. Minimum Qualifications: Years of experience: Zero-two years of related experience Degree(s): Associate degree Equivalent of experience in lieu of degree acceptable: X Yes No Professional Certification(s): N/A Strong Microsoft Office skills including Word, Outlook, PowerPoint, Excel, and Visio. Excellent verbal and written communication skills. Ability to communicate with others in a professional manner. Ability to adapt to changing priorities and manage several tasks concurrently. Exceptional organizational, planning, and time management skills. Preferred Qualifications: N/A We believe real innovation comes from inclusion - where different experiences, perspectives and talents are celebrated. So if you're wondering whether SNHU is right for you, take the leap and apply. You might be just the person we're looking for. If you have a disability and require a reasonable accommodation to fully engage in any part of the application or hiring process, please complete the Accommodation Request form or contact us at 603-626-9447. A member from the Employee Accommodation Support Center will be in contact with you within two business days to discuss your request. Compensation The hourly pay range for this position is $17.97 - $28.76. Actual offer will be based on skills, qualifications, experience and internal equity, in addition to relevant business considerations. We expect this position to be hired in the following target hiring range $19.86 - $26.86. Apply Now Save Saved Share Share Related Jobs Student - Conference Services Office Assistant Save Saved Student Jobs On-Site (New Hampshire) Student - Penmen Productions Broadcaster Save Saved Student Jobs On-Site (New Hampshire) Student - Jayme's Fund for Social Justice Development and Communications Assistant (Work-Study Only) Save Saved Student Jobs On-Site (New Hampshire) See all jobs Expect the unexpected As a university, it’s no surprise we employ many talented academics. What you may not know is that SNHU isn’t solely made up of folks with higher ed experience. Not even close. Where will your talent take you? See all teams Academics & Teaching Business Operations & Technology Campus Staff Customer Service & Student Support Human Resources & Strategy Marketing & Communications Student Jobs Don't see the job you're looking for? Connect with us anyway! We post new jobs frequently, and joining our talent community is a great way to be notified when we do. Join talent community Sitemap Cookies Corporate site Need an Accommodation? © SNHU 2026, all rights reserved. Thank you, your preferences have been updated. Manage Preferences Accept All Essential Only"
