    "https://jobs.snhu.edu/en/jobs/r0014841/student-assistive-technology-assistant/": {
      "title": "Student - Assistive Technology Assistant",
      "description": "Student - Assistive Technology Assistant,  | SNHU Careers Skip to main content Who We Are Who We Are Culture Benefits Equity, Diversity & Inclusion Military Career Areas Career Areas Online Teaching Jobs Academics & Teaching Business Operations & Technology Campus Staff Customer Service & Student Support Human Resources & Strategy Marketing & Communications Student Jobs Working at SNHU Working at SNHU Flexible Work Training & Development How We Hire 0 My Saved Jobs Search Jobs Student Jobs Student - Assistive Technology Assistant Part time October 04, 2026 On-Site (New Hampshire) Description Southern New Hampshire University is a team of innovators. World changers. Individuals who believe in progress with purpose. Since 1932, our people-centered strategy has defined us — and helped us grow a team that now serves over 180,000 learners worldwide. Our mission to transform lives is made possible by talented people who bring diverse industry experience, backgrounds and skills to the university. And today, we're ready to expand our reach. All we need is you. The opportunity Join the Assistive Technology team and gain meaningful work experience while helping others. As a Student Assistant, you will explore assistive technology, create accessible videos and job aids, support campus events and research, and connect students with free digital resources. Through this hands-on work, you will build skills in communication, teamwork, critical thinking, problem-solving, leadership, professionalism, technology, and career development. If you are curious, ready to learn, and interested in making technology easier for everyone to use, apply to join our team. In this role, you will: Communicate clearly with people who use assistive technology by listening carefully, asking helpful questions, and explaining practical strategies for work and learning. Build confidence using a variety of assistive technology tools and devices. Identify, troubleshoot, and help resolve basic assistive technology issues. Contribute ideas, gather information, and complete assigned tasks for team projects and research. Create clear, simple, and accessible job aids and other helpful resources. Build professional relationships with student clubs and campus groups. Advocate for assistive technology and promote free digital resources available to all students. Take part in training and learning opportunities about accessibility, assistive technology, and apply new knowledge to future work. Qualifications Be enrolled full-time at Southern New Hampshire University. Have a GPA of 2.5 or higher. Be comfortable using Microsoft 365 and video creation and editing platforms. Be able to learn new information and use it in your work. Be able to solve problems and troubleshoot basic issues. Be able to manage several tasks. Protect others’ privacy. Be comfortable working in a busy environment where priorities may change. Think about the needs and experience of the person using the technology. Be curious and willing to learn about new accessibility and educational technology. Be self-motivated and interested in professional growth. We believe real innovation comes from inclusion - where different experiences, perspectives and talents are celebrated. So if you're wondering whether SNHU is right for you, take the leap and apply. You might be just the person we're looking for. If you have a disability and require a reasonable accommodation to fully engage in any part of the application or hiring process, please complete the Accommodation Request form or contact us at 603-626-9447. A member from the Employee Accommodation Support Center will be in contact with you within two business days to discuss your request. Compensation The hourly pay range for this position is $13.00 - $15.00. Actual offer will be based on skills, qualifications, experience and internal equity, in addition to relevant business considerations. Apply Now Save Saved Share Share Related Jobs Student - Manchester True Collaborative Marketing and Social Media Assistant (Work-Study Only) Save Saved Student Jobs On-Site (New Hampshire) Student - Jayme's Fund for Social Justice Development and Communications Assistant (Work-Study Only) Save Saved Student Jobs On-Site (New Hampshire) Student - Robotics and Engineering Lab Assistant Save Saved Student Jobs On-Site (New Hampshire) See all jobs Expect the unexpected As a university, it’s no surprise we employ many talented academics. What you may not know is that SNHU isn’t solely made up of folks with higher ed experience. Not even close. Where will your talent take you? See all teams Academics & Teaching Business Operations & Technology Campus Staff Customer Service & Student Support Human Resources & Strategy Marketing & Communications Student Jobs Don't see the job you're looking for? Connect with us anyway! We post new jobs frequently, and joining our talent community is a great way to be notified when we do. Join talent community Sitemap Cookies Corporate site Need an Accommodation? © SNHU 2026, all rights reserved. Thank you, your preferences have been updated. Manage Preferences Accept All Essential Only"
