    "https://jobs.snhu.edu/en/jobs/r0014794/student-breakthrough-manchester-education-equity-and-impact-assistant/": {
      "title": "Student - Breakthrough Manchester Education, Equity and Impact Assistant",
      "description": "Student - Breakthrough Manchester Education, Equity and Impact Assistant,  | SNHU Careers Skip to main content Who We Are Who We Are Culture Benefits Equity, Diversity & Inclusion Military Career Areas Career Areas Online Teaching Jobs Academics & Teaching Business Operations & Technology Campus Staff Customer Service & Student Support Human Resources & Strategy Marketing & Communications Student Jobs Working at SNHU Working at SNHU Flexible Work Training & Development How We Hire 0 My Saved Jobs Search Jobs Student Jobs Student - Breakthrough Manchester Education, Equity and Impact Assistant Part time September 30, 2026 On-Site (New Hampshire) Description Southern New Hampshire University is a team of innovators. World changers. Individuals who believe in progress with purpose. Since 1932, our people-centered strategy has defined us — and helped us grow a team that now serves over 180,000 learners worldwide. Our mission to transform lives is made possible by talented people who bring diverse industry experience, backgrounds and skills to the university. And today, we're ready to expand our reach. All we need is you. The opportunity Southern New Hampshire University is seeking a student employee to fill the role of Education, Equity and Impact Assistant for our partner organization Breakthrough Manchester in Manchester, NH. Are you passionate about educational equity, youth empowerment, and making a real impact? Join the team at Breakthrough Manchester, where college students, like you, help shape the next generation of changemakers! Breakthrough’s one-of-a-kind students-teaching-students model provides six years of tuition-free academic programming for Manchester students from marginalized communities and inspires high school and college students to become the next wave of educators, advocates, and leaders. We’re looking for a creative, motivated intern to join our small but mighty year-round team. You’ll play a key role in marketing, communications, event planning, and helping us share Breakthrough’s impact and shape our future. The assistant is responsible for managing and supporting various aspects of this non-profit educational organization. The person who fills this position will receive significant training and support and is expected to become autonomous in successfully achieving duties. This is an opportunity to gain hands-on professional experience while making a meaningful impact in your community. As an Education, Equity and Impact Assistant you’ll work alongside Breakthrough Staff and educators, contribute to real projects, and develop skills in various areas of non-profit operations. Job Responsibilities Communications & Social Media: Express your creativity by developing content for BTM’s social platforms; Event Management: Build confidence by planning, preparing for, and supporting special events and regular Saturday programming; Education & Programming: Assist with teacher training events and program sessions to get an inside look at how educational programs are created while building connections with education professionals; Administrative Support: Gain clerical experience by preparing materials for program activities and supporting staff with day to day administrative tasks such as mailing, printing, and filing; Data Tracking & Organization: Take charge in the retrieval and organization of confidential student and academic information while developing strong organizational and professional skills; Leadership: Find your voice by leading group activities, taking on meaningful responsibilities, solving problems, and learning how to turn your ideas into action. Why you’ll love it: Gain hands-on experience in marketing, education, and non-profit management Work with a fun, passionate team that values creativity, collaboration, and equity Build skills that make your résumé stand out and make a real difference in your community Minimum Qualifications Current enrollment in classes as part of a SNHU degree program Work study part of financial aid package Students with work study may be prioritized Reliable transportation preferred, not required (this site is only about a 10-15 minute walk down the street) The ideal candidate: Aligns with Breakthrough’s mission statement Open and accepting of people of all backgrounds Sensitive to issues that affect access to higher education Has an outstanding record of academic and professional achievements Is very organized and self-motivated Has effective verbal and written communication skills towards people of all ages Committed to learning and growing in a rewarding, fast-paced work environment Positive, high-energy, can-do spirit; resilience and perseverance Candidates with fluency in Spanish, Vietnamese, Bosnian, or other languages are encouraged to apply. Proficiency with the Google Suite of applications, social media platforms, and Canva preferred Learning Outcomes (NACE Competencies) Develop Communication skills through professional interactions with staff, faculty, and scholars. Develop Equity & Inclusion awareness by interacting respectfully with diverse populations. Strengthen Teamwork skills by collaborating with colleagues. Build Professionalism through reliability, accountability, and workplace etiquette. Improve Critical Thinking by solving problems and making informed decisions in daily tasks. Practice Leadership by taking initiative and supporting Breakthrough goals. Increase Career & Self-Development through workplace experience and professional growth. Work Schedule 10 hours per week for the school year (excluding school vacation). Office hours are Monday-Friday 08:00am-4:00pm. Willingness to work some evenings and weekends. We believe real innovation comes from inclusion - where different experiences, perspectives and talents are celebrated. So if you're wondering whether SNHU is right for you, take the leap and apply. You might be just the person we're looking for. If you have a disability and require a reasonable accommodation to fully engage in any part of the application or hiring process, please complete the Accommodation Request form or contact us at 603-626-9447. A member from the Employee Accommodation Support Center will be in contact with you within two business days to discuss your request. Compensation The hourly pay range for this position is $13.00 - $15.00. Actual offer will be based on skills, qualifications, experience and internal equity, in addition to relevant business considerations. Apply Now Save Saved Share Share Related Jobs Student - Robotics and Engineering Lab Assistant Save Saved Student Jobs On-Site (New Hampshire) Student - Manchester True Collaborative Center Administration Assistant (Work-Study Only) Save Saved Student Jobs On-Site (New Hampshire) Student - UpReach Assistant to the Program Director (Work-Study Only) Save Saved Student Jobs On-Site (New Hampshire) See all jobs Expect the unexpected As a university, it’s no surprise we employ many talented academics. What you may not know is that SNHU isn’t solely made up of folks with higher ed experience. Not even close. Where will your talent take you? See all teams Academics & Teaching Business Operations & Technology Campus Staff Customer Service & Student Support Human Resources & Strategy Marketing & Communications Student Jobs Don't see the job you're looking for? Connect with us anyway! We post new jobs frequently, and joining our talent community is a great way to be notified when we do. Join talent community Sitemap Cookies Corporate site Need an Accommodation? © SNHU 2026, all rights reserved. Thank you, your preferences have been updated. Manage Preferences Accept All Essential Only"
