    "https://jobs.snhu.edu/en/jobs/r0014759/stats-entry-coordinator/": {
      "title": "Stats Entry Coordinator",
      "description": "Stats Entry Coordinator,  | SNHU Careers Skip to main content Who We Are Who We Are Culture Benefits Equity, Diversity & Inclusion Military Career Areas Career Areas Online Teaching Jobs Academics & Teaching Business Operations & Technology Campus Staff Customer Service & Student Support Human Resources & Strategy Marketing & Communications Student Jobs Working at SNHU Working at SNHU Flexible Work Training & Development How We Hire 0 My Saved Jobs Search Jobs Athletics Stats Entry Coordinator Part time September 21, 2026 On-Site (New Hampshire) Description Southern New Hampshire University is a team of innovators. World changers. Individuals who believe in progress with purpose. Since 1932, our people-centered strategy has defined us — and helped us grow a team that now serves over 180,000 learners worldwide. Our mission to transform lives is made possible by talented people who bring diverse industry experience, backgrounds and skills to the university. And today, we're ready to expand our reach. All we need is you. This position is based in the following office location: Manchester, NH The opportunity Job Description Southern New Hampshire University's traditional campus is looking for a Stats Entry Coordinator to keep track of statistics live during SNHU sporting events. You will be on-site and report to the Director of Athletic Communication and your objective is to provide us with insight into the performance of athletes and teams by producing statistical data that can be interpreted by coaches, trainers, athletes, and fans. \"#LI-On-site\" In this Role You'll Get To: Produce statistical data that can be used by the athletic department for further analysis You will need a desire to learn and in an athletic environment Work in collaboration with our Director of Athletic Communication and other members of the Athletic Department. What we're Looking For: 1+ years of experience in the game of volleyball and an understanding of the rules and regulations Use NCAA Live Stats software; willing to train and upskill with this software Night and weekend availability following game schedules We believe real innovation comes from inclusion - where different experiences, perspectives and talents are celebrated. So if you're wondering whether SNHU is right for you, take the leap and apply. You might be just the person we're looking for. If you have a disability and require a reasonable accommodation to fully engage in any part of the application or hiring process, please complete the Accommodation Request form or contact us at 603-626-9447. A member from the Employee Accommodation Support Center will be in contact with you within two business days to discuss your request. Compensation The hourly pay range for this position is $14.86 - $23.79. Actual offer will be based on skills, qualifications, experience and internal equity, in addition to relevant business considerations. We expect this position to be hired in the following target hiring range $16.43 - $22.23. Apply Now Save Saved Share Share Related Jobs Student - Athletic Social Media Assistant Save Saved Student Jobs On-Site (New Hampshire) Part-Time Assistant Track and Field Coach Save Saved Athletics On-Site (New Hampshire) Student - Penmen Productions Broadcaster Save Saved Student Jobs On-Site (New Hampshire) See all jobs Expect the unexpected As a university, it’s no surprise we employ many talented academics. What you may not know is that SNHU isn’t solely made up of folks with higher ed experience. Not even close. Where will your talent take you? See all teams Academics & Teaching Business Operations & Technology Campus Staff Customer Service & Student Support Human Resources & Strategy Marketing & Communications Student Jobs Don't see the job you're looking for? Connect with us anyway! We post new jobs frequently, and joining our talent community is a great way to be notified when we do. Join talent community Sitemap Cookies Corporate site Need an Accommodation? © SNHU 2026, all rights reserved. Thank you, your preferences have been updated. Manage Preferences Accept All Essential Only"
