    "https://jobs.snhu.edu/en/jobs/r0014628/part-time-assistant-track-and-field-coach/": {
      "title": "Part-Time Assistant Track and Field Coach",
      "description": "Part-Time Assistant Track and Field Coach,  | SNHU Careers Skip to main content Who We Are Who We Are Culture Benefits Equity, Diversity & Inclusion Military Career Areas Career Areas Online Teaching Jobs Academics & Teaching Business Operations & Technology Campus Staff Customer Service & Student Support Human Resources & Strategy Marketing & Communications Student Jobs Working at SNHU Working at SNHU Flexible Work Training & Development How We Hire 0 My Saved Jobs Search Jobs Athletics Part-Time Assistant Track and Field Coach Part time September 17, 2026 On-Site (New Hampshire) Description Southern New Hampshire University is a team of innovators. World changers. Individuals who believe in progress with purpose. Since 1932, our people-centered strategy has defined us — and helped us grow a team that now serves over 180,000 learners worldwide. Our mission to transform lives is made possible by talented people who bring diverse industry experience, backgrounds and skills to the university. And today, we're ready to expand our reach. All we need is you. This position is based in the following office location: Manchester, NH The opportunity Southern New Hampshire University (SNHU), a NCAA DII institution and proud member of the Northeast-10 Conference, is excited to invite applications for the position of Part-Time Assistant Track & Field Coach. You will report to the Director of Cross-Country and Track and Field and implement training programs for multi-events, throwing events, or other field events . (SNHU does not field a men's track & field team.) Work Hours: 10-20 hours per week. Practice times can vary depending on the season and athlete class schedule, but we ask that you are able to travel and work variable hours, including nights and weekends for some competitions. What you'll do: Plan and lead daily training sessions for the throwing events, including warm-up routines, technical drills and aid in the strength program. Develop personalized training plans to help athlete's achieve their goals. Provide guidance and feedback to athletes on proper techniques during training and at competitions. Motivate athletes to achieve their goals in a supportive and positive environment. Help us recruit specific student-athletes involved in throwing events. Work with other coaches, staff, and administrators to ensure the success of the track and field program. Provide mentorship and support for student-athletes, focusing on their academic, athletic, and personal development. Ensure compliance with all NCAA, NE10 Conference, and SNHU policies and regulations. What we're looking for: 1+ years coaching and/or personal athletic experience in multi-events, throwing events, or other field events. Bachelor's degree or 3+ years of coaching experience in multi-events, throwing events, or other field events. Hold a valid driver's license and be eligible to be insured by the university's auto insurance carrier to drive team vans to competitions when needed. #LI-Onsite We believe real innovation comes from inclusion - where different experiences, perspectives and talents are celebrated. So if you're wondering whether SNHU is right for you, take the leap and apply. You might be just the person we're looking for. If you have a disability and require a reasonable accommodation to fully engage in any part of the application or hiring process, please complete the Accommodation Request form or contact us at 603-626-9447. A member from the Employee Accommodation Support Center will be in contact with you within two business days to discuss your request. Compensation The hourly pay range for this position is $14.86 - $23.79. Actual offer will be based on skills, qualifications, experience and internal equity, in addition to relevant business considerations. We expect this position to be hired in the following target hiring range $16.43 - $22.23. Apply Now Save Saved Share Share Related Jobs Part-time Volleyball Club Coach Save Saved