    "https://jobs.snhu.edu/en/jobs/r0014596/student-athletic-audio-visual-assistant/": {
      "title": "Student-Athletic Audio Visual Assistant",
      "description": "Student-Athletic Audio Visual Assistant,  | SNHU Careers Skip to main content Who We Are Who We Are Culture Benefits Equity, Diversity & Inclusion Military Career Areas Career Areas Online Teaching Jobs Academics & Teaching Business Operations & Technology Campus Staff Customer Service & Student Support Human Resources & Strategy Marketing & Communications Student Jobs Working at SNHU Working at SNHU Flexible Work Training & Development How We Hire 0 My Saved Jobs Search Jobs Student Jobs Student-Athletic Audio Visual Assistant Part time September 12, 2026 On-Site (New Hampshire) Description Southern New Hampshire University is a team of innovators. World changers. Individuals who believe in progress with purpose. Since 1932, our people-centered strategy has defined us — and helped us grow a team that now serves over 180,000 learners worldwide. Our mission to transform lives is made possible by talented people who bring diverse industry experience, backgrounds and skills to the university. And today, we're ready to expand our reach. All we need is you. The opportunity Job Summary Southern New Hampshire University is currently seeking a Student Worker as an Athletics Audio Visual Assistant, for our Athletic Department located on campus. This position will work closely with our Athletic Teams, and film games and practices throughout the season. The video will get uploaded into our conference mandated film exchange. Along with film, this position will DJ athletic contests, including pre-game music as well as in-game and post-game music. Job Responsibilities -Film ALL HOME GAMES-Mens and Women's Basketball, Hockey -Assist in managing automated cameras for Men's and Women's Soccer, Field Hockey, Volleyball, Men's and Women's Lacrosse -Upload film and manage league mandated Film Exchange -Act as DJ for athletic contests-pre-game music, in game music, post game music -Assist in office work including music management, film breakdown, etc Minimum Qualifications Current enrollment in classes as part of a SNHU degree program Work study part of financial aid package Students with work study may be prioritized General Knowledge of Athletics, Video, and Music Passion to learn Learning Outcomes (NACE Competencies) Develop Communication skills through professional interactions with students, staff, and faculty. Strengthen Teamwork skills by collaborating with department staff and fellow student employees. Build Professionalism through reliability, accountability, and workplace etiquette. Enhance Technology skills through the use of office systems, software, or specialized tools. Improve Critical Thinking by solving problems and making informed decisions in daily tasks. Practice Leadership by taking initiative and supporting departmental goals. Increase Career & Self-Development through workplace experience and professional growth. Develop Equity & Inclusion awareness by interacting respectfully with diverse populations. Work Schedule This role varies in hours dependent on athletic contest schedule. Nights and weekend are required due to the nature of games and schedules of teams. Generally, hours range from 10-15 hours per week. Additional Information We believe real innovation comes from inclusion - where different experiences, perspectives and talents are celebrated. So if you're wondering whether SNHU is right for you, take the leap and apply. You might be just the person we're looking for. If you have a disability and require a reasonable accommodation to fully engage in any part of the application or hiring process, please complete the Accommodation Request form or contact us at 603-626-9447. A member from the Employee Accommodation Support Center will be in contact with you within two business days to discuss your request. Compensation The hourly pay range for this position is $13.00 - $15.00. Actual offer will be based on skills, qualifications, experience and internal equity, in addition to relevant business considerations. Apply Now Save Saved Share Share Related Jobs Student - Athletics Game Day and Equipment Supervisor Save Saved Student Jobs On-Site (New Hampshire) Student - Penmen Productions Broadcaster Save Saved Student Jobs On-Site (New Hampshire) Student - UpReach Assistant to the Program Director (Work-Study Only) Save Saved Student Jobs On-Site (New Hampshire) See all jobs Expect the unexpected As a university, it’s no surprise we employ many talented academics. What you may not know is that SNHU isn’t solely made up of folks with higher ed experience. Not even close. Where will your talent take you? See all teams Academics & Teaching Business Operations & Technology Campus Staff Customer Service & Student Support Human Resources & Strategy Marketing & Communications Student Jobs Don't see the job you're looking for? Connect with us anyway! We post new jobs frequently, and joining our talent community is a great way to be notified when we do. Join talent community Sitemap Cookies Corporate site Need an Accommodation? © SNHU 2026, all rights reserved. Thank you, your preferences have been updated. Manage Preferences Accept All Essential Only"
