    "https://jobs.snhu.edu/en/jobs/r0014679/student-nh-audubon-animal-care-specialist-work-study-only/": {
      "title": "Student - NH Audubon Animal Care Specialist (Work-Study Only)",
      "description": "Student - NH Audubon Animal Care Specialist (Work-Study Only),  | SNHU Careers Skip to main content Who We Are Who We Are Culture Benefits Equity, Diversity & Inclusion Military Career Areas Career Areas Online Teaching Jobs Academics & Teaching Business Operations & Technology Campus Staff Customer Service & Student Support Human Resources & Strategy Marketing & Communications Student Jobs Working at SNHU Working at SNHU Flexible Work Training & Development How We Hire 0 My Saved Jobs Search Jobs Student Jobs Student - NH Audubon Animal Care Specialist (Work-Study Only) Part time September 12, 2026 On-Site (New Hampshire) Description Southern New Hampshire University is a team of innovators. World changers. Individuals who believe in progress with purpose. Since 1932, our people-centered strategy has defined us — and helped us grow a team that now serves over 180,000 learners worldwide. Our mission to transform lives is made possible by talented people who bring diverse industry experience, backgrounds and skills to the university. And today, we're ready to expand our reach. All we need is you. The opportunity Southern New Hampshire University is seeking a student employee to fill the role of Animal Care Specialist for our partner organization New Hampshire Audubon. Under direct supervision of the Animal Programs Curator, perform animal care duties for the animal ambassador collection at NH Audubon’s Massabesic Center. Support environmental education efforts to enhance visitor experiences while promoting our mission to protect New Hampshire’s environment for wildlife and for people. Job Responsibilities Perform all aspects of animal husbandry, including but not limited to cleaning enclosures, preparing diet and feeding animals, providing behavioral and environmental enrichment devices, handling animals, observing behavior, monitoring animal health, keeping records, and participating in animal training for husbandry purposes. Interact with and answer questions for visitors, including school groups and the general public, in a professional and friendly manner to generate excitement for the natural world via hands-on artifacts and materials in the Nature Lab. Minimum Qualifications Current enrollment in classes as part of a SNHU degree program Work study part of financial aid package Students with work study may be prioritized Reliable transportation Some animal husbandry experience preferred. Knowledge of caring for reptiles, amphibians, invertebrates, and/or aquatic tanks preferred. Knowledge of New Hampshire wildlife and environmental concepts preferred. Comfort with talking to the general public and working with children required. Must have the ability to bend, stoop, and lift up to 25 lbs. Will provide training to the right candidate. Learning Outcomes (NACE Competencies) Students will gain experience with best practices in animal husbandry related to reptiles, amphibians, aquatic wildlife, and invertebrates. Students will learn environmental education concepts and teaching methods. Students will improve customer service and communication skills and will glean insight into non-profit organization operations. Work Schedule Sun-Tues 10am-1pm, Weds-Sat 11am-5pm. This position is designed to be shared between two employees who will work alternate, sometimes overlapping shifts, up to 20 hours per week for each employee. We believe real innovation comes from inclusion - where different experiences, perspectives and talents are celebrated. So if you're wondering whether SNHU is right for you, take the leap and apply. You might be just the person we're looking for. If you have a disability and require a reasonable accommodation to fully engage in any part of the application or hiring process, please complete the Accommodation Request form or contact us at 603-626-9447. A member from the Employee Accommodation Support Center will be in contact with you within two business days to discuss your request. Compensation The hourly pay range for this position is $13.00 - $15.00. Actual offer will be based on skills, qualifications, experience and internal equity, in addition to relevant business considerations. Apply Now Save Saved Share Share Related Jobs Student - UpReach Assistant to the Program Director (Work-Study Only) Save Saved Student Jobs On-Site (New Hampshire) Student - Building Communities in NH Marketing Program Assistant (Work-Study Only) Save Saved Student Jobs On-Site (New Hampshire) Student - 21st Century Program Support Staff (Work-Study Only) Save Saved Student Jobs On-Site (New Hampshire) See all jobs Expect the unexpected As a university, it’s no surprise we employ many talented academics. What you may not know is that SNHU isn’t solely made up of folks with higher ed experience. Not even close. Where will your talent take you? See all teams Academics & Teaching Business Operations & Technology Campus Staff Customer Service & Student Support Human Resources & Strategy Marketing & Communications Student Jobs Don't see the job you're looking for? Connect with us anyway! We post new jobs frequently, and joining our talent community is a great way to be notified when we do. Join talent community Sitemap Cookies Corporate site Need an Accommodation? © SNHU 2026, all rights reserved. Thank you, your preferences have been updated. Manage Preferences Accept All Essential Only"
    },
    "https://jobs.snhu.edu/en/jobs/r0014644/student-penmen-guide-co-leader/": {
      "title": "Student- Alumni Engagement Assistant",
      "description": "Student - Penmen Guide Co-Leader,  | SNHU Careers Skip to main content Who We Are Who We Are Culture Benefits Equity, Diversity & Inclusion Military Career Areas Career Areas Online Teaching Jobs Academics & Teaching Business Operations & Technology Campus Staff Customer Service & Student Support Human Resources & Strategy Marketing & Communications Student Jobs Working at SNHU Working at SNHU Flexible Work Training & Development How We Hire 0 My Saved Jobs Search Jobs Student Jobs Student - Penmen Guide Co-Leader Part time September 12, 2026 On-Site (New Hampshire) Description Southern New Hampshire University is a team of innovators. World changers. Individuals who believe in progress with purpose. Since 1932, our people-centered strategy has defined us — and helped us grow a team that now serves over 180,000 learners worldwide. Our mission to transform lives is made possible by talented people who bring diverse industry experience, backgrounds and skills to the university. And today, we're ready to expand our reach. All we need is you. The opportunity Southern New Hampshire University is seeking a student employee to fill the role of Penmen Guide Co-Leader. The Penmen Guide Co-Leader supports the leadership, training, and daily operations of the Penmen Guide team. Responsibilities include coordinating schedules, recruiting and onboarding guides, facilitating meetings and training, providing coaching and feedback, supporting campus events and special visits, and serving as a communication liaison between guides and Admissions leadership. Co-Leaders help foster team engagement, maintain high-quality campus tours, and continuously improve the visitor experience. Job Responsibilities: Coordinate and maintain the year-round Penmen Guide tour and office schedule, ensuring appropriate staffing and coverage. Support the recruitment, interviewing, selection, onboarding, and development of new Penmen Guides. Plan and facilitate bi-weekly Penmen Guide meetings, including agendas, announcements, training, and important updates. Serve as a communication liaison between Penmen Guides, the Leadership Team, and Admissions staff. Develop and facilitate training for new and returning guides and maintain accurate, up-to-date training materials and the Tour Guide Manual. Conduct evaluation tours and provide constructive feedback to help guides strengthen their communication, public speaking, tour delivery, and professionalism. Support golf cart training and safety procedures for Penmen Guides. Meet regularly with the Penmen Guide Supervisor and Leadership Team to discuss operations, challenges, and opportunities for improvement. Coordinate Penmen Guide staffing for Admissions events, group tours, VIP visits, and other campus visit programs. Collaborate with Admissions staff and the Pro Staff Event Coordinator to support event preparation, logistics, and execution. Conduct regular check-ins with Penmen Guides to provide support, gather feedback, and encourage professional growth. Develop initiatives that promote team engagement, morale, collaboration, and a positive team environment. Identify and implement opportunities to improve tour guide operations and enhance the campus visit experience. Minimum Qualifications: Must be a current undergraduate or graduate student at the university. Minimum of one semester of experience as a Penmen Guide. Demonstrated leadership, organization, communication, and teamwork skills. Ability to serve as a positive leader, mentor, and role model. Professional demeanor and ability to represent the Admissions Office and university positively. Ability to manage time commitments and maintain a flexible schedule, including potential part-time availability in August for training and preparation. Ability to collaborate effectively and share responsibilities with the Penmen Guide Leadership Team. Valid driver's license required/preferred for responsibilities that may involve transportation or campus-related tasks. Learning Outcomes: As a Penmen Guide Co-Leader, you’ll have the opportunity to develop real-world leadership, communication, event planning, and organizational skills while helping shape the experience of future Penmen. You’ll work closely with Admissions professionals and fellow student leaders to support your team and make an impact on the campus visit experience. We believe real innovation comes from inclusion - where different experiences, perspectives and talents are celebrated. So if you're wondering whether SNHU is right for you, take the leap and apply. You might be just the person we're looking for. If you have a disability and require a reasonable accommodation to fully engage in any part of the application or hiring process, please complete the Accommodation Request form or contact us at 603-626-9447. A member from the Employee Accommodation Support Center will be in contact with you within two business days to discuss your request. Compensation The hourly pay range for this position is $13.00 - $15.00. Actual offer will be based on skills, qualifications, experience and internal equity, in addition to relevant business considerations. Apply Now Save Saved Share Share Related Jobs Student-Student Access Leader Save Saved Student Jobs On-Site (New Hampshire) Student- Alumni Engagement Assistant Save Saved Student Jobs On-Site (New Hampshire) Student - Penmen Productions Broadcaster Save Saved Student Jobs On-Site (New Hampshire) See all jobs Expect the unexpected As a university, it’s no surprise we employ many talented academics. What you may not know is that SNHU isn’t solely made up of folks with higher ed experience. Not even close. Where will your talent take you? See all teams Academics & Teaching Business Operations & Technology Campus Staff Customer Service & Student Support Human Resources & Strategy Marketing & Communications Student Jobs Don't see the job you're looking for? Connect with us anyway! We post new jobs frequently, and