    "https://jobs.snhu.edu/en/jobs/r0014587/student-penmen-productions-assistant/": {
      "title": "Student - Penmen Productions Assistant",
      "description": "Student - Penmen Productions Assistant,  | SNHU Careers Skip to main content Who We Are Who We Are Culture Benefits Equity, Diversity & Inclusion Military Career Areas Career Areas Online Teaching Jobs Academics & Teaching Business Operations & Technology Campus Staff Customer Service & Student Support Human Resources & Strategy Marketing & Communications Student Jobs Working at SNHU Working at SNHU Flexible Work Training & Development How We Hire 0 My Saved Jobs Search Jobs Student Jobs Student - Penmen Productions Assistant Part time September 12, 2026 On-Site (New Hampshire) Description Southern New Hampshire University is a team of innovators. World changers. Individuals who believe in progress with purpose. Since 1932, our people-centered strategy has defined us — and helped us grow a team that now serves over 180,000 learners worldwide. Our mission to transform lives is made possible by talented people who bring diverse industry experience, backgrounds and skills to the university. And today, we're ready to expand our reach. All we need is you. The opportunity The opportunity Southern New Hampshire University is currently seeking a student employee to fill the role of Penmen Productions Assistant for our Campus location. Penmen Productions is the Southern New Hampshire University Athletics’ video entity. In collaboration with the Department of Athletic Communications, Penmen Productions oversees video streaming, video features, video replay and manages relationships with local and national television providers. The department is most notably known for its production of live online video streaming, video features and live game broadcasts. Essential Duties and Responsibilities: Serving as a camera operator during athletics contests Creating in-game and post-game highlight packages Serving as a producer and technical director of game broadcasts and assisting the Athletics Communications staff at home contests. Other duties include operating the in-game graphics generator, Ouellette Stadium video board, conducting interviews with student-athletes and coaches, and the set up and break down of broadcast equipment. Serving as Reply Operator for Board Show and Broadcast. Minimum Qualifications: Enrollment in an Undergraduate or Graduate Day program at SNHU Preferred Qualifications: Previous video and broadcast experience preferred, but not required Knowledge/passion for sports Willingness to learn Night & weekend availability is required Work Hours: Games, as scheduled. Office hours, as needed. Total number of hours per week not to exceed 20 hours per week. Required Documents: Please provide your class schedule along with a resume or a purpose statement detailing qualifications and interest in the role. We believe real innovation comes from inclusion - where different experiences, perspectives and talents are celebrated. So if you're wondering whether SNHU is right for you, take the leap and apply. You might be just the person we're looking for. If you have a disability and require a reasonable accommodation to fully engage in any part of the application or hiring process, please complete the Accommodation Request form or contact us at 603-626-9447. A member from the Employee Accommodation Support Center will be in contact with you within two business days to discuss your request. Compensation The hourly pay range for this position is $13.00 - $15.00. Actual offer will be based on skills, qualifications, experience and internal equity, in addition to relevant business considerations. Apply Now Save Saved Share Share Related Jobs Student - Penmen Productions Broadcaster Save Saved Student Jobs On-Site (New Hampshire) Student - Athletic Social Media Assistant Save Saved Student Jobs On-Site (New Hampshire) Student - Penmen Guide Co-Leader Save Saved Student Jobs On-Site (New Hampshire) See all jobs Expect the unexpected As a university, it’s no surprise we employ many talented academics. What you may not know