    "https://jobs.snhu.edu/en/jobs/r0014531/student-student-involvementstudent-affairs-staff-assistant-work-study-only/": {
      "title": "Student - Student Involvement/Student Affairs Staff Assistant (Work-Study Only)",
      "description": "Student - Student Involvement/Student Affairs Staff Assistant (Work-Study Only),  | SNHU Careers Skip to main content Who We Are Who We Are Culture Benefits Equity, Diversity & Inclusion Military Career Areas Career Areas Online Teaching Jobs Academics & Teaching Business Operations & Technology Campus Staff Customer Service & Student Support Human Resources & Strategy Marketing & Communications Student Jobs Working at SNHU Working at SNHU Flexible Work Training & Development How We Hire 0 My Saved Jobs Search Jobs Student Jobs Student - Student Involvement/Student Affairs Staff Assistant (Work-Study Only) Part time September 12, 2026 On-Site (New Hampshire) Description Southern New Hampshire University is a team of innovators. World changers. Individuals who believe in progress with purpose. Since 1932, our people-centered strategy has defined us — and helped us grow a team that now serves over 180,000 learners worldwide. Our mission to transform lives is made possible by talented people who bring diverse industry experience, backgrounds and skills to the university. And today, we're ready to expand our reach. All we need is you. The opportunity Student Involvement/Student Affairs Staff Assistants play a vital role in fostering a welcoming and inclusive campus environment by delivering high-quality customer service to students, staff, and guests of Southern New Hampshire University (SNHU). In this role, student employees will support the daily operations of the Office of Student Involvement and the Office of Student Affairs through administrative and customer service tasks, event support, and special projects. This position provides a unique opportunity for students to develop career-readiness skills while helping to build a vibrant, engaging, and inclusive campus community. Job Responsibilities Career & Self-Development / Professionalism Serve as the first point of contact for the office, welcoming and assisting visitors with professionalism and care Perform administrative tasks including scheduling via Microsoft Outlook, answering phones, managing shared email accounts, scanning, filing, and data entry Maintain confidentiality and demonstrate responsible behavior while handling sensitive information Adhere to dress code and arrive on time for scheduled shifts Communication Answer telephone calls clearly and courteously; take accurate messages and direct inquiries appropriately Communicate effectively with students, staff, and faculty in both written and verbal formats Teamwork / Leadership Collaborate with staff and fellow student employees on departmental events such as Orientation, Opening Weekend, and Homecoming Attend monthly staff meetings and participate in staff development and appreciation events Critical Thinking Demonstrate initiative and problem-solving skills when managing tasks or addressing visitor needs Work independently with minimal supervision and manage multiple responsibilities effectively Equity & Inclusion Contribute to an inclusive office culture by valuing diverse perspectives and supporting engagement opportunities that foster a sense of belonging for all students Participate in training that supports equity, inclusion, and cultural awareness Minimum Qualifications Must be enrolled full-time in an Undergraduate or Graduate Day Program at SNHU Work Study part of financial aid package Students with work study may be prioritized Strong interpersonal, organizational, and communication skills Comfortable using Microsoft Office tools and handling telephone communications Ability to work flexible hours, including occasional nights and weekends Learning Outcomes (NACE Competencies) Student employees will gain hands-on experience and skill development aligned with NACE Career Readiness Competencies through on-the-job learning, monthly one-on-one training sessions, departmental training events, and conference participation. As part of the Student Involvement/Student Affairs team, you will develop in the following core areas: Community – Cultivate a welcoming environment that fosters connection and student engagement Continual Improvement – Embrace feedback and engage in reflection to grow personally and professionally Inclusivity – Promote and support programming that reflects the diverse needs of our student body Integrity – Uphold ethical standards and demonstrate authenticity in your work Teamwork – Foster collaboration and mutual support in a dynamic team environment Work Schedule Student employees are typically scheduled to work 10-15 hours per week during the academic year. Office hours are Monday through Friday, 8:00 a.m. – 6:00 p.m. Work schedules will be determined based on the student's class schedule and departmental needs, with flexibility to support academic commitments. Ability to work occasional evenings and weekends is required to assist with departmental events and programs. Student employees are expected to attend monthly staff meetings and participate in staff development and appreciation events as part of their employment. We believe real innovation comes from inclusion - where different experiences, perspectives and talents are celebrated. So if you're wondering whether SNHU is right for you, take the leap and apply. You might be just the person we're looking for. If you have a disability and require a reasonable accommodation to fully engage in any part of the application or hiring process, please complete the Accommodation Request form or contact us at 603-626-9447. A member from the Employee Accommodation Support Center will be in contact with you within two business days to discuss your request. Compensation The hourly pay range for this position is $13.00 - $15.00. Actual offer will be based on skills, qualifications, experience and internal equity, in addition to relevant business considerations. Apply Now Save Saved Share Share Related Jobs Student - 21st Century Program Support Staff (Work-Study Only) Save Saved Student Jobs On-Site (New Hampshire) Student - Manchester True Collaborative Marketing and Social Media Assistant (Work-Study Only) Save Saved Student Jobs On-Site (New Hampshire) Student - Building Communities in NH Marketing Program Assistant (Work-Study Only) Save Saved Student Jobs On-Site (New Hampshire) See all jobs Expect the unexpected As a university, it’s no surprise we employ many talented academics. What you may not know is that SNHU isn’t solely made up of folks with higher ed experience. Not even close. Where will your talent take you? See all teams Academics & Teaching Business Operations & Technology Campus Staff Customer Service & Student Support Human Resources & Strategy Marketing & Communications Student Jobs Don't see the job you're looking for? Connect with us anyway! We post new jobs frequently, and joining our talent community is a great way to be notified when we do. Join talent community Sitemap Cookies Corporate site Need an Accommodation? © SNHU 2026, all rights reserved. Thank you, your preferences have been updated. Manage Preferences Accept All Essential Only"
