    "https://jobs.snhu.edu/en/jobs/r0014561/student-campus-major-ambassador/": {
      "title": "Student - Robotics and Engineering Lab Assistant",
      "description": "Student - Campus Major Ambassador,  | SNHU Careers Skip to main content Who We Are Who We Are Culture Benefits Equity, Diversity & Inclusion Military Career Areas Career Areas Online Teaching Jobs Academics & Teaching Business Operations & Technology Campus Staff Customer Service & Student Support Human Resources & Strategy Marketing & Communications Student Jobs Working at SNHU Working at SNHU Flexible Work Training & Development How We Hire 0 My Saved Jobs Search Jobs Student Jobs Student - Campus Major Ambassador Part time September 12, 2026 On-Site (New Hampshire) Description Southern New Hampshire University is a team of innovators. World changers. Individuals who believe in progress with purpose. Since 1932, our people-centered strategy has defined us — and helped us grow a team that now serves over 180,000 learners worldwide. Our mission to transform lives is made possible by talented people who bring diverse industry experience, backgrounds and skills to the university. And today, we're ready to expand our reach. All we need is you. The opportunity Job Summary Southern NH University is seeking student employees to fill the role of Major Ambassadors. Major Ambassadors are upper-class student mentors who can help first-year students experience a relentless welcome to their major. We will be hiring two major ambassadors for certain majors SNHU offers on-campus. The following Majors will be considered: Justice Studies, Education, Game, Business Administration, Psychology, English, Engineering, Biology. Major Ambassadors will attend events that are unique to the major, will connect with freshmen and will facilitate workshops and sessions dedicated to first-year students. A Major Ambassador’s job is to make sure an incoming student meets the faculty and those who support the field, so students have a constellation of support on campus within their first year. Please note: You must be invited by a faculty member to participate in this program. Job Responsibilities Demonstrate professionalism and teamwork while working in close collaboration with a Full-time faculty in your major. Use leadership and communication skills by creating and promoting events for students in the major. Show career and self-development during events meant to welcome students to their field of study (science, humanities). Demonstrate inclusion and equity by facilitating workshops prior to registration for new students in the major. Other duties, responsibilities or activities may be assigned at any time. Minimum Qualification Enrollment in an Undergraduate On-Campus Day program at SNHU. Must be an upper-class student enrolled in a degree program at SNHU Highly dependable and flexible. Attendance, punctuality, and reliability are essential functions of this role. Must have an endorsement from any faculty member in the department where the student wishes to be a major ambassador. Learning Outcomes (NACE Competencies) Develop Communication skills through professional interactions with students, staff, and faculty. Strengthen Teamwork skills by collaborating with department staff and fellow student employees. Build Professionalism through reliability, accountability, and workplace etiquette. Enhance Technology skills through the use of office systems, software, or specialized tools. Improve Critical Thinking by solving problems and making informed decisions in daily tasks. Practice Leadership by taking initiative and supporting departmental goals. Increase Career & Self-Development through workplace experience and professional growth. Develop Equity & Inclusion awareness by interacting respectfully with diverse populations. Work Schedule As a Major Ambassador, you will work an average of 2 hours per week. Some weeks there will be no hours, and if an event is planned, some weeks there will be 5-10 hours. This averages out to 2 hours per week. We believe real innovation comes from inclusion - where different experiences, perspectives and talents are celebrated. So if you're wondering whether SNHU is right for you, take the leap and apply. You might be just the person we're looking for. If you have a disability and require a reasonable accommodation to fully engage in any part of the application or hiring process, please complete the Accommodation Request form or contact us at 603-626-9447. A member from the Employee Accommodation Support Center will be in contact with you within two business days to discuss your request. Compensation The hourly pay range for this position is $13.00 - $15.00. Actual offer will be based on skills, qualifications, experience and internal equity, in addition to relevant business considerations. Apply Now Save Saved Share Share Related Jobs Student-Conference Services Setup Crew Member Save Saved Student Jobs On-Site (New Hampshire) Student - Robotics and Engineering Lab Assistant Save Saved Student Jobs On-Site (New Hampshire) Student- Alumni Engagement Assistant Save Saved Student Jobs On-Site (New Hampshire) See all jobs Expect the unexpected As a university, it’s no surprise we employ many talented academics. What you may not know is that SNHU isn’t solely made up of folks with higher ed experience. Not even close. Where will your talent take you? See all teams Academics & Teaching Business Operations & Technology Campus Staff Customer Service & Student Support Human Resources & Strategy Marketing & Communications Student Jobs Don't see the job you're looking for? Connect with us anyway! We post new jobs frequently, and joining our talent community is a great way to be notified when we do. Join talent community Sitemap Cookies Corporate site Need an Accommodation? © SNHU 2026, all rights reserved. Thank you, your preferences have been updated. Manage Preferences Accept All Essential Only"
    },
    "https://jobs.snhu.edu/en/jobs/r0014681/student-safe-sports-network-social-media-and-marketing-assistant-work-study-only/": {
      "title": "Student - Safe Sports Network Social Media and Marketing Assistant (Work-Study Only)",
      "description": "Student - Safe Sports Network Social Media and Marketing Assistant (Work-Study Only),  | SNHU Careers Skip to main content Who We Are Who We Are Culture Benefits Equity, Diversity & Inclusion Military Career Areas Career Areas Online Teaching Jobs Academics & Teaching Business Operations & Technology Campus Staff Customer Service & Student Support Human Resources & Strategy Marketing & Communications Student Jobs Working at SNHU Working at SNHU Flexible Work Training & Development How We Hire 0 My Saved Jobs Search Jobs Student Jobs Student - Safe Sports Network Social Media and Marketing Assistant (Work-Study Only) Part time September 12, 2026 On-Site (New Hampshire) Description Southern New Hampshire University is a team of innovators. World changers. Individuals who believe in progress with purpose. Since 1932, our people-centered strategy has defined us — and helped us grow a team that now serves over 180,000 learners worldwide. Our mission to transform lives is made possible by talented people who bring diverse industry experience, backgrounds and skills to the university. And today, we're ready to expand our reach. All we need is you. The opportunity Southern New Hampshire University is seeking a student employee to fill the role of Social Media and Marketing Assistant for our partner organization, Safe Sports Network. The assistant supports Safe Sports Network with its social media and marketing programs. In collaboration with the Development and Communications Manager you will be responsible for supporting marketing and communications on our social media platforms (Facebook, Instagram, and others) and the creation of digital assets, including travel to off-site locations to collect video and photo media. Job Responsibilities The work will include various media tasks, including collecting video recordings and taking photographs for media content. Tasks will require travel to off-site locations (i.e. schools during practice and game times). Support creation of materials (photos, videos, etc.) for social media platforms; May include posting on social media platforms. Collaborate with Development and Communications Manager on projects and events, including communications to donors, student ambassadors, and other volunteers. Help with creation of digital and printed collateral including event materials, direct mail, newsletters, and infographics. Assist with developing and collecting content for monthly e-newsletters and quarterly impact videos, including actually recording videos and taking photographs for use in materials. Support tracking of metrics on social media platforms (Facebook, Instagram, YouTube). Perform other duties as assigned by staff managers. Minimum Qualifications Current enrollment in classes as part of a SNHU degree program Work study part of financial aid package Students with work study may be prioritized Reliable transportation Interest in social media, video content, and photography General knowledge and/or enthusiasm for the program mission of Safe Sports Network Learning Outcomes (NACE Competencies) Exposure to video, photo and other media creation and dissemination Improvement with communication skills Increase experience with logistics and event planning Hone organizational and time management skills Gain exposure and knowledge of inner workings of non-profit organizations Work Schedule Flexible, with afternoons preferred M-F; plus occasional special events; Approx. 10-12 hours/week. We believe real innovation comes from inclusion - where different experiences, perspectives and talents are celebrated. So if you're wondering whether SNHU is right for you, take the leap and apply. You might be just the person we're looking for. If you have a disability and require a reasonable accommodation to fully engage in any part of the application or hiring process, please complete the Accommodation Request form or contact us at 603-626-9447. A member from the Employee Accommodation Support Center will be in contact with you within two business days to discuss your request. Compensation The hourly pay range for this position is $13.00 - $15.00. Actual offer will be based on skills, qualifications, experience and internal equity, in addition to relevant business considerations. Apply Now Save Saved Share Share Related Jobs Student - Building Communities in NH Marketing Program Assistant (Work-Study Only) Save Saved Student Jobs On-Site (New Hampshire) Student - Jayme's Fund for Social Justice Development and Communications Assistant (Work-Study Only) Save Saved Student Jobs On-Site (New Hampshire) Student - Safe Sports Network Administrative/Volunteer Program Assistant (Work-Study Only) Save Saved Student Jobs On-Site (New Hampshire) See all jobs Expect the unexpected As a university, it’s no surprise we employ many talented academics. What you may not know is that SNHU isn’t solely made up of folks with higher ed experience. Not even close. Where will your talent take you? See all teams Academics & Teaching Business Operations & Technology Campus Staff Customer Service & Student Support Human Resources & Strategy Marketing & Communications Student Jobs Don't see the job you're looking for? Connect with us anyway! We post new jobs frequently, and joining our talent community is a great way to be notified when we do. Join talent community Sitemap Cookies Corporate site Need an Accommodation? © SNHU 2026, all rights reserved. Thank you, your preferences have been updated. Manage Preferences Accept All Essential Only"
    },
    "https://jobs.snhu.edu/en/jobs/r0014643/student-penmen-guide/": {
      "title": "Student - Manchester True Collaborative Marketing and Social Media Assistant (Work-Study Only)",
      "description": "Student - Penmen Guide,  | SNHU Careers Skip to main content Who We Are Who We Are Culture Benefits Equity, Diversity & Inclusion Military Career Areas Career Areas Online Teaching Jobs Academics & Teaching Business Operations & Technology Campus Staff Customer Service & Student Support Human Resources & Strategy Marketing & Communications Student Jobs Working at SNHU Working at SNHU Flexible Work Training & Development How We Hire 0 My Saved Jobs Search Jobs Student Jobs Student - Penmen Guide Part time September 12, 2026 On-Site (New Hampshire) Description Southern New Hampshire University is a team of innovators. World changers. Individuals who believe in progress with purpose. Since 1932, our people-centered strategy has defined us — and helped us grow a team that now serves over 180,000 learners worldwide. Our mission to transform lives is made possible by talented people who bring diverse industry experience, backgrounds and skills to the university. And today, we're ready to expand our reach. All we need is you. The opportunity The SNHU Admissions Office is seeking strong student leaders for the Penmen Tour Guide position. This position plays a crucial role in representing the university to prospective students, their families, and other visitors. This position involves providing engaging and informative tours of the campus, sharing personal experiences, and answering questions to help visitors gain a comprehensive understanding of the university's offerings, culture, and environment. Key Responsibilities: Conduct Campus Tours: Lead groups of prospective students, families, and other visitors on tours of the campus. Provide detailed and accurate information about campus facilities, academic programs, student services, and campus life. Tailor tours to the interests and needs of different groups. Engage and Inform Visitors: Share personal experiences and insights about being a student at SNHU Answer questions from visitors in a knowledgeable and friendly manner. Highlight unique aspects and strengths of SNHU Represent the University Serve as an ambassador for SNHU, embodying its values and mission. Maintain a professional and approachable demeanor at all times. Promote a positive image of SNHU to all visitors. Assist with Events: Assist Admission Counselors in prepping and working special events such as Open Houses, Accepted Student Days, and more. Stay Informed: Keep up-to-date with the latest information about university programs, policies, and events. Participate in training sessions and meetings to enhance tour guiding skills and knowledge. Administrative Duties: Assist with administrative tasks related to office projects and event preparation. Qualifications: Current Student Status: Must be a current undergraduate or graduate student at the university. Communication Skills: Excellent verbal communication and public speaking skills. Interpersonal Skills: Friendly, approachable, and able to interact effectively with diverse groups of people. Knowledge: Familiarity with the university's campus, programs, services, and student life. Reliability: Punctual, dependable, and able to manage time effectively. Flexibility: Willingness to work flexible hours, including some weekends and evenings. Enthusiasm: Passionate about the university and eager to share that enthusiasm with others. Preferred Qualifications: Students with Federal Work Study are preferred. Prior experience in a customer service or public-facing role. Involvement in campus activities, organizations, or leadership roles. Work Environment: This position involves significant walking and outdoor activity in various weather conditions. Tours may require standing and speaking for extended periods. Average weekly hours range from 5-12 hours / week We believe real innovation comes from inclusion - where different experiences, perspectives and talents are celebrated. So if you're wondering whether SNHU is right for you, take the leap and apply. You might be just the person we're looking for. If you have a disability and require a reasonable accommodation to fully engage in any part of the application or hiring process, please complete the Accommodation Request form or contact us at 603-626-9447. A member from the Employee Accommodation Support Center will be in contact with you within two business days to discuss your request. Compensation The hourly pay range for this position is $13.00 - $15.00. Actual offer will be based on skills, qualifications, experience and internal equity, in addition to relevant business considerations. Apply Now Save Saved Share Share Related Jobs Student - Residence Life Sustainability Liaison Student Eco Rep Save Saved Student Jobs On-Site (New Hampshire) Student - Penmen Guide Co-Leader Save Saved Student Jobs On-Site (New Hampshire) Student - Manchester True Collaborative Marketing and Social Media Assistant (Work-Study Only) Save Saved Student Jobs On-Site (New Hampshire) See all jobs Expect the unexpected As a university, it’s no surprise we employ many talented academics. What you may not know is that SNHU isn’t solely made up of folks with higher ed experience. Not even close. Where will your talent take you? See all teams Academics & Teaching Business Operations & Technology Campus Staff Customer Service & Student Support Human Resources & Strategy Marketing & Communications Student Jobs Don't see the job you're looking for? Connect with us anyway! We post new jobs frequently, and joining our talent community is a great way to be notified when we do. Join talent community Sitemap Cookies Corporate site Need an Accommodation? © SNHU 2026, all rights reserved. Thank you, your preferences have been updated. Manage Preferences Accept All Essential Only"
    },
    "https://jobs.snhu.edu/en/jobs/r0014684/student-upreach-mounted-program-assistant-work-study-only/": {
      "title": "Student - UpReach Mounted Program Assistant (Work-Study Only)",
      "description": "Student - UpReach Mounted Program Assistant (Work-Study Only),  | SNHU Careers Skip to main content Who We Are Who We Are Culture Benefits Equity, Diversity & Inclusion Military Career Areas Career Areas Online Teaching Jobs Academics & Teaching Business Operations & Technology Campus Staff Customer Service & Student Support Human Resources & Strategy Marketing & Communications Student Jobs Working at SNHU Working at SNHU Flexible Work Training & Development How We Hire 0 My Saved Jobs Search Jobs Student Jobs Student - UpReach Mounted Program Assistant (Work-Study Only) Part time September 12, 2026 On-Site (New Hampshire) Description Southern New Hampshire University is a team of innovators. World changers. Individuals who believe in progress with purpose. Since 1932, our people-centered strategy has defined us — and helped us grow a team that now serves over 180,000 learners worldwide. Our mission to transform lives is made possible by talented people who bring diverse industry experience, backgrounds and skills to the university. And today, we're ready to expand our reach. All we need is you. The opportunity Southern New Hampshire University is seeking a student employee to fill the role of Mounted Program Assistant for our partner organization, UpReach Therapeutic Equestrian Center in Goffstown, NH. The program assistant will gain a wide variety of experience in program support, volunteer management, disabilities awareness, general horse care, therapeutic riding/driving lesson planning, as well as providing direct support to individuals with disabilities. As a program assistant, you will have the opportunity to be involved in multiple areas to experience the daily functions of a nonprofit organization. All mounted program assistants must completed a volunteer training session as well as Taking the Lead training. Prior horse experience is not required. Job Responsibilities Provide direct support to participants in therapeutic riding and therapeutic driving lessons and hippotherapy sessions. Learn about disabilities and disability awareness, choosing words with dignity and person-first language. Participate in a variety of administrative tasks including data entry. Support the organizations mission. Minimum Qualifications Current enrollment in classes as part of a SNHU degree program Work study part of financial aid package Students with work study may be prioritized Reliable transportation Experience with Microsoft Suite, especially Word, Excel and PowerPoint is preferred Effective written and oral communication Demonstrate professionalism and maintain confidentiality with participants, volunteers and staff ​ Learning Outcomes (NACE Competencies) Students will gain knowledge and experience working with individuals with cognitive and physical disabilities Learn how a nonprofit operates and flourishes Time management Leadership Work Schedule Flexible scheduling, open Monday-Friday We believe real innovation comes from inclusion - where different experiences, perspectives and talents are celebrated. So if you're wondering whether SNHU is right for you, take the leap and apply. You might be just the person we're looking for. If you have a disability and require a reasonable accommodation to fully engage in any part of the application or hiring process, please complete the Accommodation Request form or contact us at 603-626-9447. A member from the Employee Accommodation Support Center will be in contact with you within two business days to discuss your request. Compensation The hourly pay range for this position is $13.00 - $15.00. Actual offer will be based on skills, qualifications, experience and internal equity, in addition to relevant business considerations. Apply Now Save Saved Share Share Related Jobs Student - Animal Rescue League of NH Shelter Assistant (Work-Study Only) Save Saved Student Jobs On-Site (New Hampshire) Student - UpReach Non-Profit Management Assistant (Work-Study Only) Save Saved Student Jobs On-Site (New Hampshire) Student - UpReach Assistant to the Program Director (Work-Study Only) Save Saved Student Jobs On-Site (New Hampshire) See all jobs Expect the unexpected As a university, it’s no surprise we employ many talented academics. What you may not know is that SNHU isn’t solely made up of folks with higher ed experience. Not even close. Where will your talent take you? See all teams Academics & Teaching Business Operations & Technology Campus Staff Customer Service & Student Support Human Resources & Strategy Marketing & Communications Student Jobs Don't see the job you're looking for? Connect with us anyway! We post new jobs frequently, and joining our talent community is a great way to be notified when we do. Join talent community Sitemap Cookies Corporate site Need an Accommodation? © SNHU 2026, all rights reserved. Thank you, your preferences have been updated. Manage Preferences Accept All Essential Only"
    },
    "https://jobs.snhu.edu/en/jobs/r0014496/student-athletics-game-day-and-equipment-staff/": {
      "title": "Student - Athletic Social Media Assistant",
      "description": "Student - Athletics Game Day and Equipment Staff,  | SNHU Careers Skip to main content Who We Are Who We Are Culture Benefits Equity, Diversity & Inclusion Military Career Areas Career Areas Online Teaching Jobs Academics & Teaching Business Operations & Technology Campus Staff Customer Service & Student Support Human Resources & Strategy Marketing & Communications Student Jobs Working at SNHU Working at SNHU Flexible Work Training & Development How We Hire 0 My Saved Jobs Search Jobs Student Jobs Student - Athletics Game Day and Equipment Staff Part time September 12, 2026 On-Site (New Hampshire) Description Southern New Hampshire University is a team of innovators. World changers. Individuals who believe in progress with purpose. Since 1932, our people-centered strategy has defined us — and helped us grow a team that now serves over 180,000 learners worldwide. Our mission to transform lives is made possible by talented people who bring diverse industry experience, backgrounds and skills to the university. And today, we're ready to expand our reach. All we need is you. The opportunity Southern New Hampshire University is seeking student employees to fill the role of Athletics Game Day and Equipment Staff. This position assists with the day-to-day operations of the athletic department- from managing numerous duties for all of our on-campus contests to the daily activities of practices and laundry for all SNHU Athletic teams. Job Responsibilities: Assist with the game operations of all on campus contests, in various locations - Larkin, athletic complex, Penmen stadium, tennis, as well as baseball and softball fields. assisting with security, scoreboard, tickets, and other areas as needed. Packing game bags, team laundry, practice management Other duties as assigned by student supervisors, or operations staff. Minimum Qualifications: Current enrollment in classes as part of a SNHU degree program Work study part of financial aid package Students with work study may be prioritized We believe real innovation comes from inclusion - where different experiences, perspectives and talents are celebrated. So if you're wondering whether SNHU is right for you, take the leap and apply. You might be just the person we're looking for. If you have a disability and require a reasonable accommodation to fully engage in any part of the application or hiring process, please complete the Accommodation Request form or contact us at 603-626-9447. A member from the Employee Accommodation Support Center will be in contact with you within two business days to discuss your request. Compensation The hourly pay range for this position is $13.00 - $15.00. Actual offer will be based on skills, qualifications, experience and internal equity, in addition to relevant business considerations. Apply Now Save Saved Share Share Related Jobs Student - Athletics Game Day and Equipment Supervisor Save Saved Student Jobs On-Site (New Hampshire) Student - Penmen Productions Broadcaster Save Saved Student Jobs On-Site (New Hampshire) Student - Athletic Social Media Assistant Save Saved Student Jobs On-Site (New Hampshire) See all jobs Expect the unexpected As a university, it’s no surprise we employ many talented academics. What you may not know is that SNHU isn’t solely made up of folks with higher ed experience. Not even close. Where will your talent take you? See all teams Academics & Teaching Business Operations & Technology Campus Staff Customer Service & Student Support Human Resources & Strategy Marketing & Communications Student Jobs Don't see the job you're looking for? Connect with us anyway! We post new jobs frequently, and joining our talent community is a great way to be notified when we do. Join talent community Sitemap Cookies Corporate site Need an Accommodation? © SNHU 2026, all rights reserved. Thank you, your preferences have been updated. Manage Preferences Accept All Essential Only"
