    "https://jobs.snhu.edu/en/jobs/r0014674/student-building-communities-in-nh-marketing-program-assistant-work-study-only/": {
      "title": "Student - Building Communities in NH Marketing Program Assistant (Work-Study Only)",
      "description": "Student - Building Communities in NH Marketing Program Assistant (Work-Study Only),  | SNHU Careers Skip to main content Who We Are Who We Are Culture Benefits Equity, Diversity & Inclusion Military Career Areas Career Areas Online Teaching Jobs Academics & Teaching Business Operations & Technology Campus Staff Customer Service & Student Support Human Resources & Strategy Marketing & Communications Student Jobs Working at SNHU Working at SNHU Flexible Work Training & Development How We Hire 0 My Saved Jobs Search Jobs Student Jobs Student - Building Communities in NH Marketing Program Assistant (Work-Study Only) Part time September 12, 2026 On-Site (New Hampshire) Description Southern New Hampshire University is a team of innovators. World changers. Individuals who believe in progress with purpose. Since 1932, our people-centered strategy has defined us — and helped us grow a team that now serves over 180,000 learners worldwide. Our mission to transform lives is made possible by talented people who bring diverse industry experience, backgrounds and skills to the university. And today, we're ready to expand our reach. All we need is you. The opportunity Southern New Hampshire University is seeking a student employee to fill the role of Marketing Program Assistant for our partner organization, Building Communities in New Hampshire in Manchester, NH. Support Building Community in New Hampshire's marketing and communications efforts by creating and posting social media content (Facebook, Instagram, LinkedIn), maintaining the website, drafting the e-newsletter, and providing general office support. This role includes occasional on-site event coverage to capture photos and video for the organization's marketing channels. Job Responsibilities Create and publish engaging content for the organization's social media platforms, including photos, graphics, and short videos. Photograph and record video footage in the office and at occasional community events to support social media and marketing content. Update and maintain content on the organization's website, including program pages, event listings, and photos. Draft copy for the organization's e-newsletter and coordinate with staff to gather content. Provide general office support, including research and assisting staff with administrative tasks. Attend occasional community events to gather content and represent the organization in a professional manner. Organize and maintain a digital library of photos, videos, and marketing materials for ongoing use. Collaborate with the Executive Director to ensure marketing materials align with the organization's brand and mission. Minimum Qualifications: Current enrollment in classes as part of a SNHU degree program Work study part of financial aid package Students with work study may be prioritized Reliable transportation Comfortable using a smartphone or camera to take photos and record and edit video. Experience with social media platforms such as Instagram and Facebook. Strong written communication and proofreading skills. Reliable, punctual, and detail-oriented. Able to work both independently and as part of a team. Preferred (not required): experience with Canva, WordPress, or similar content tools; interest in marketing or nonprofit communications. ​ Learning Outcomes (NACE Competencies) Develop Communication skills through professional interactions with students, staff, and faculty. Strengthen Teamwork skills by collaborating with department staff and fellow student employees. Build Professionalism through reliability, accountability, and workplace etiquette. Improve Critical Thinking by solving problems and making informed decisions in daily tasks. Increase Career & Self-Development through workplace experience and professional growth. Work Schedule 20 hours/week; specific days/hours arranged with supervisor around the student's class schedule We believe real innovation comes from inclusion - where different experiences, perspectives and talents are celebrated. So if you're wondering whether SNHU is right for you, take the leap and apply. You might be just the person we're looking for. If you have a disability and require a reasonable accommodation to fully engage in any part of the application or hiring process, please complete the Accommodation Request form or contact us at 603-626-9447. A member from the Employee Accommodation Support Center will be in contact with you within two business days to discuss your request. Compensation The hourly pay range for this position is $13.00 - $15.00. Actual offer will be based on skills, qualifications, experience and internal equity, in addition to relevant business considerations. Apply Now Save Saved Share Share Related Jobs Student - Jayme's Fund for Social Justice Development and Communications Assistant (Work-Study Only) Save Saved Student Jobs On-Site (New Hampshire) Student - Safe Sports Network Social Media and Marketing Assistant (Work-Study Only) Save Saved Student Jobs On-Site (New Hampshire) Student - Manchester True Collaborative Marketing and Social Media Assistant (Work-Study Only) Save Saved Student Jobs On-Site (New Hampshire) See all jobs Expect the unexpected As a university, it’s no surprise we employ many talented academics. What you may not know is that SNHU isn’t solely made up of folks with higher ed experience. Not even close. Where will your talent take you? See all teams Academics & Teaching Business Operations & Technology Campus Staff Customer Service & Student Support Human Resources & Strategy Marketing & Communications Student Jobs Don't see the job you're looking for? Connect with us anyway! We post new jobs frequently, and joining our talent community is a great way to be notified when we do. Join talent community Sitemap Cookies Corporate site Need an Accommodation? © SNHU 2026, all rights reserved. Thank you, your preferences have been updated. Manage Preferences Accept All Essential Only"
