      "title": "Part-Time Assistant Baseball Coach",
      "description": "Part-time Volleyball Club Coach,  | SNHU Careers Skip to main content Who We Are Who We Are Culture Benefits Equity, Diversity & Inclusion Military Career Areas Career Areas Online Teaching Jobs Academics & Teaching Business Operations & Technology Campus Staff Customer Service & Student Support Human Resources & Strategy Marketing & Communications Student Jobs Working at SNHU Working at SNHU Flexible Work Training & Development How We Hire 0 My Saved Jobs Search Jobs Athletics Part-time Volleyball Club Coach Part time September 12, 2026 On-Site (New Hampshire) Description Southern New Hampshire University is a team of innovators. World changers. Individuals who believe in progress with purpose. Since 1932, our people-centered strategy has defined us — and helped us grow a team that now serves over 180,000 learners worldwide. Our mission to transform lives is made possible by talented people who bring diverse industry experience, backgrounds and skills to the university. And today, we're ready to expand our reach. All we need is you. This position is based in the following office location: Manchester, NH The opportunity Southern New Hampshire University's traditional campus in Manchester, NH is looking for a part-time Women's Volleyball Club Coach. You will instruct the club according to the level of each club member, developing skills ranging from beginner to advanced. In this position, you will report to the Assistant Director of Campus Recreation. What You'll do: You will coach the club according to the SNHU rules and all applicable associations as set forth by the Sports Club Handbook Understand all emergency and safety procedures on equipment, rental and travel management observing the Sports Club Handbook You will conduct all practices and games while remaining in consideration of guidelines in the Sports Club Handbook. Mentor all members of your team while helping the executive board accomplish goals Support and give us guidance in recruiting new members to participate and join the club Attend all practices and competitions Arrive on time and organize practice sessions Be present for all mandatory training sessions as instructed by the University and Campus Recreation Department. You will need to guide communication between players and Club Sport Administrative staff. Instruct all participants on proper technique and ways to improve in the given sport You will be a chaperone for all travel games and must act observing all travel guidelines as set forth by the Office of Student Involvement What we're Looking For: 1+ years of coaching experience in the sport of volleyball and experience managing a team High School diploma Current CPR/First Aid certification (We will train if current certification is not held) Current valid driver's license and ability to be an approved authorized driver for the University #LI-Onsite We believe real innovation comes from inclusion - where different experiences, perspectives and talents are celebrated. So if you're wondering whether SNHU is right for you, take the leap and apply. You might be just the person we're looking for. If you have a disability and require a reasonable accommodation to fully engage in any part of the application or hiring process, please complete the Accommodation Request form or contact us at 603-626-9447. A member from the Employee Accommodation Support Center will be in contact with you within two business days to discuss your request. Compensation The hourly pay range for this position is $13.51 - $21.62. Actual offer will be based on skills, qualifications, experience and internal equity, in addition to relevant business considerations. We expect this position to be hired in the following target hiring range $14.94 - $20.20. Apply Now Save Saved Share Share Related Jobs Part-Time Assistant Baseball Coach Save Saved Athletics On-Site (New Hampshire) Part-time Club Dance Coach Save Saved Athletics On-Site (New Hampshire) Student - Intramural 