elopment, finance short and long term strategic planning and development Minimum Qualifications ​Current enrollment in classes as part of a SNHU degree program Work study part of financial aid package Students with work study may be prioritized Reliable transportation Must have working knowledge of Microsoft Office applications Main professionalism Possess a strong work ethic Have excellent written and verbal communication skills Interest in nonprofit/small business administration Learning Outcomes (NACE Competencies) Student will learn firsthand the challenges, successes and rewards of working at a nonprofit organization. Work Schedule Flexible scheduling between Monday through Friday We believe real innovation comes from inclusion - where different experiences, perspectives and talents are celebrated. So if you're wondering whether SNHU is right for you, take the leap and apply. You might be just the person we're looking for. If you have a disability and require a reasonable accommodation to fully engage in any part of the application or hiring process, please complete the Accommodation Request form or contact us at 603-626-9447. A member from the Employee Accommodation Support Center will be in contact with you within two business days to discuss your request. Compensation The hourly pay range for this position is $13.00 - $15.00. Actual offer will be based on skills, qualifications, experience and internal equity, in addition to relevant business considerations. Apply Now Save Saved Share Share Related Jobs Student - Building Communities in NH Marketing Program Assistant (Work-Study Only) Save Saved Student Jobs On-Site (New Hampshire) Student - Jayme's Fund for Social Justice Development and Communications Assistant (Work-Study Only) Save Saved Student Jobs On-Site (New Hampshire) Student - UpReach Mounted Program Assistant (Work-Study Only) Save Saved Student Jobs On-Site (New Hampshire) See all jobs Expect the unexpected As a university, it’s no surprise we employ many talented academics. What you may not know is that SNHU isn’t solely made up of folks with higher ed experience. Not even close. Where will your talent take you? See all teams Academics & Teaching Business Operations & Technology Campus Staff Customer Service & Student Support Human Resources & Strategy Marketing & Communications Student Jobs Don't see the job you're looking for? Connect with us anyway! We post new jobs frequently, and joining our talent community is a great way to be notified when we do. Join talent community Sitemap Cookies Corporate site Need an Accommodation? © SNHU 2026, all rights reserved. Thank you, your preferences have been updated. Manage Preferences Accept All Essential Only"
