imum Qualifications Current enrollment in classes as part of a SNHU degree program Work study part of financial aid package Students with work study may be prioritized Reliable transportation Learning Outcomes (NACE Competencies) Students will gain knowledge of working in a school setting and through collaboration gain experience in supervising/mentoring youth. Build Professionalism through reliability, accountability, and workplace etiquette. Strengthen Teamwork skills by collaborating with department staff and fellow student employees. Work Schedule Flexible based on interest. Generally within Manchester Public Schools, Monday - Friday 2:45-5pm We believe real innovation comes from inclusion - where different experiences, perspectives and talents are celebrated. So if you're wondering whether SNHU is right for you, take the leap and apply. You might be just the person we're looking for. If you have a disability and require a reasonable accommodation to fully engage in any part of the application or hiring process, please complete the Accommodation Request form or contact us at 603-626-9447. A member from the Employee Accommodation Support Center will be in contact with you within two business days to discuss your request. Compensation The hourly pay range for this position is $13.00 - $15.00. Actual offer will be based on skills, qualifications, experience and internal equity, in addition to relevant business considerations. Apply Now Save Saved Share Share Related Jobs Student - UpReach Assistant to the Program Director (Work-Study Only) Save Saved Student Jobs On-Site (New Hampshire) Student - Study Away Operational Assistant Save Saved Student Jobs On-Site (New Hampshire) Student - Jayme's Fund for Social Justice Development and Communications Assistant (Work-Study Only) Save Saved Student Jobs On-Site (New Hampshire) See all jobs Expect the unexpected As a university, it’s no surprise we employ many talented academics. What you may not know is that SNHU isn’t 