    "https://jobs.snhu.edu/en/jobs/r0014443/student-lead-peer-educator/": {
      "title": "Academics & Teaching",
      "description": "Student - Lead Peer Educator,  | SNHU Careers Skip to main content Who We Are Who We Are Culture Benefits Equity, Diversity & Inclusion Military Career Areas Career Areas Online Teaching Jobs Academics & Teaching Business Operations & Technology Campus Staff Customer Service & Student Support Human Resources & Strategy Marketing & Communications Student Jobs Working at SNHU Working at SNHU Flexible Work Training & Development How We Hire 0 My Saved Jobs Search Jobs Student Jobs Student - Lead Peer Educator Part time September 12, 2026 On-Site (New Hampshire) Description Southern New Hampshire University is a team of innovators. World changers. Individuals who believe in progress with purpose. Since 1932, our people-centered strategy has defined us — and helped us grow a team that now serves over 180,000 learners worldwide. Our mission to transform lives is made possible by talented people who bring diverse industry experience, backgrounds and skills to the university. And today, we're ready to expand our reach. All we need is you. The opportunity Southern New Hampshire University is seeking a student employee to fill the role of Lead Peer Tutor. The Lead Peer Educator serves as a mentor, tutor, and team leader within the Peer Education program. In this role, the Lead Peer Educator supports tutees in specific content areas while mentoring new tutors and assisting in training, team building, and program development. Lead Peer Educators model best practices in tutoring, communication, professionalism, and inclusive engagement. This position is designed to further enhance student workers’ leadership, tutoring expertise, and career readiness while contributing to SNHU’s learning community. Essential Duties and Responsibilities: Serve as a mentor and role model to new and current peer tutors; assist with onboarding, training, and professional development efforts. Assist coordinator(s) with discipline-specific training, conduct class visits, in-class sessions, class-embedded assignments, and other special projects as assigned. Assist coordinator(s) with organizing team meetings, workshops, or training sessions that foster collaboration, equity, and continuous learning. Assist with WLC office opening and required evening closing responsibilities. Continue with student support roles as assigned, which may include drop-in tutoring, one-to-one tutoring, review sessions, and class-embedded assignments. Provide advanced academic support in specific subject areas using differentiated, learner-centered strategies based on individual strengths, learning styles, backgrounds, and prior knowledge. Attend required All-Peer Educator training sessions. Check office communications daily for assignments, announcements, and correspondence. Submit payroll hours and tracking forms promptly after each shift. Support WLC annual goals and initiatives. Engage in regular communication and one-on-one meetings with tutoring coordinator. Interpersonal Expectations Motivate students and help them develop confidence through positive feedback on areas of improvement Demonstrate and coach others on strong study strategies, motivational techniques, and academic success habits consistent with tutor training. Communicate clearly and professionally with students, staff, and team members, modeling interpersonal and intercultural communication. Apply critical thinking and leadership skills to resolve issues and promote a supportive and inclusive learning environment. Use appropriate academic technologies and tools to support peer tutoring, session documentation, and professional communication. Minimum Qualifications: A minimum of one year of tutoring service at the Wolak Learning Center Current enrollment as a part/full-time SNHU student Cumulative SNHU GPA of 3.0 or higher Excellent level of responsibility, reliability, and punctuality Strong leadership and interpersonal communication skills Ease in relating to students from diverse backgrounds Learning Outcomes: Strengthen leadership skills that prepare student workers for post-graduate employment and professional advancement. Incorporate advanced communication skills in peer tutoring relationships, supporting clear, respectful dialogue. Evaluate and adapt tutoring strategies based on learner feedback, session dynamics, and academic goals. Practice inclusive tutoring ensuring all students feel welcomed, supported, and respected regardless of background or identity. Take initiative in supporting the peer educator team, mentor others, and actively contribute to a positive team culture. Model punctuality, ethical responsibility, and accountability, setting a standard for others within the program. Collaborate with fellow peer educators and staff to coordinate programming and uphold the goals of the Wolak Learning Center. Use learning platforms and communication tools to support students and peer educators across various tutoring modalities. Work Hours: Hours vary. Office Hours: Mondays-Thursdays: 9:00am-6:00pm, Fridays: 9:00am-4:30pm, closed: Saturdays and Sundays We believe real innovation comes from inclusion - where different experiences, perspectives and talents are celebrated. So if you're wondering whether SNHU is right for you, take the leap and apply. You might be just the person we're looking for. If you have a disability and require a reasonable accommodation to fully engage in any part of the application or hiring process, please complete the Accommodation Request form or contact us at 603-626-9447. A member from the Employee Accommodation Support Center will be in contact with you within two business days to discuss your request. Compensation The hourly pay range for this position is $13.00 - $15.00. Actual offer will be based on skills, qualifications, experience and internal equity, in addition to relevant business considerations. Apply Now Save Saved Share Share Related Jobs Student - Peer Tutor Save Saved Student Jobs On-Site (New Hampshire) Student-Conference Services Setup Crew Member Save Saved Student Jobs On-Site (New Hampshire) Student - Penmen Guide Co-Leader Save Saved Student Jobs On-Site (New Hampshire) See all jobs Expect the unexpected As a university, it’s no surprise we employ many talented academics. What you may not know is that SNHU isn’t solely made up of folks with higher ed experience. Not even close. Where will your talent take you? See all teams Academics & Teaching Business Operations & Technology Campus Staff Customer Service & Student Support Human Resources & Strategy Marketing & Communications Student Jobs Don't see the job you're looking for? Connect with us anyway! We post new jobs frequently, and joining our talent community is a great way to be notified when we do. Join talent community Sitemap Cookies Corporate site Need an Accommodation? © SNHU 2026, all rights reserved. Thank you, your preferences have been updated. Manage Preferences Accept All Essential Only"
    },
    "https://jobs.snhu.edu/en/jobs/r0014512/student-wllc-concierge-desk-staff/": {
      "title": "Academics & Teaching",
      "description": "Student - WLLC Concierge Desk Staff,  | SNHU Careers Skip to main content Who We Are Who We Are Culture Benefits Equity, Diversity & Inclusion Military Career Areas Career Areas Online Teaching Jobs Academics & Teaching Business Operations & Technology Campus Staff Customer Service & Student Support Human Resources & Strategy Marketing & Communications Student Jobs Working at SNHU Working at SNHU Flexible Work Training & Development How We Hire 0 My Saved Jobs Search Jobs Student Jobs Student - WLLC Concierge Desk Staff Part time September 12, 2026 On-Site (New Hampshire) Description Southern New Hampshire University is a team of innovators. World changers. Individuals who believe in progress with purpose. Since 1932, our people-centered strategy has defined us — and helped us grow a team that now serves over 180,000 learners worldwide. Our mission to transform lives is made possible by talented people who bring diverse industry experience, backgrounds and skills to the university. And today, we're ready to expand our reach. All we need is you. The opportunity Job Summary Concierge Desk staff provide high-quality customer service to the Southern New Hampshire University community. Responsibilities include answering questions and assisting with event set-ups within the Student Center and Wolak Library Learning Commons. Employees must be willing to work flexible hours, late nights and weekends. This position also supports the Office of Student Involvement in general, and employees may participate in special projects as assigned. Our student employees are essential in helping us build community and support others finding a sense of belonging at SNHU. The Concierge Desk position plays a vital role in that goal. We look to hire students who demonstrate integrity. ​ Job Responsibilities Oversee the daily operations of the Concierge Desk. Report Lost and Found items and notify person if possible. Assist students, staff, faculty, and visitors with questions and refer them to the appropriate resources. Lend out resources like, phone chargers, games, and/or office supplies as requested by students. Receive, sign for and contact student, faculty and staff regarding special deliveries (flowers, etc.) Maintain an accurate record of all transactions and duties performed Post daily signage for the Student Center and Green Center reserved tables and conference rooms Ensure meeting rooms are reset to designated format and help with special setup needs for groups Responsible for reporting security issues to Public Safety as needed while on duty Oversee and maintain rounds operations, including data collection and distribution to campus stakeholders. SGA Driver approval (preferred). Provide care for the (3) SGA SUVs including but not limited to, supporting routine maintenance, snow removal, and gas refills. Perform other duties as assigned. Expectations: Provide world class customer service Must be self-motivated and able to work independently, or with a team throughout difficult situations with little supervision Maintain a positive attitude during all shifts and be a role model for colleagues Arrive at all shifts on-time and stay until the end of the shift Wear appropriately designated and provided attire Attend all monthly staff meetings and employee appreciation events Must be committed to creating and supporting an inclusive community Minimum Qualifications Must be a full-time enrolled student in an Undergraduate Day or Graduate Day Program Must be able to climb stairs, sit, stoop, walk and carry 50 lbs. as needed. Students with work study may be prioritized Learning Goals: Students working in the Office of Student Involvement will deepen their understanding around the 5 values through learning that will take place on the job, through the opportunity to attend conferences, monthly individual staff training, department semester trainings and celebrations. These values are: Community: Fostering a sense of belonging through intentional engagement opportunities C ontinual Improvement: Assessing and evaluating to strive for personal and programmatic growth Inclusivity: Providing opportunities for the diverse needs and interests of our community Integrity: Operating in a manner marked by honesty and authenticity Teamwork: Cultivating an atmosphere of supportive interdependence We believe real innovation comes from inclusion - where different experiences, perspectives and talents are celebrated. So if you're wondering whether SNHU is right for you, take the leap and apply. You might be just the person we're looking for. If you have a disability and require a reasonable accommodation to fully engage in any part of the application or hiring process, please complete the Accommodation Request form or contact us at 603-626-9447. A member from the Employee Accommodation Support Center will be in contact with you within two business days to discuss your request. Compensation The hourly pay range for this position is $13.00 - $15.00. Actual offer will be based on skills, qualifications, experience and internal equity, in addition to relevant business considerations. Apply Now Save Saved Share Share Expect the unexpected As a university, it’s no surprise we employ many talented academics. What you may not know is that SNHU isn’t solely made up of folks with higher ed experience. Not even close. Where will your talent take you? See all teams Academics & Teaching Business Operations & Technology Campus Staff Customer Service & Student Support Human Resources & Strategy Marketing & Communications Student Jobs Don't see the job you're looking for? Connect with us anyway! We post new jobs frequently, and joining our talent community is a great way to be notified when we do. Join talent community Sitemap Cookies Corporate site Need an Accommodation? © SNHU 2026, all rights reserved. Thank you, your preferences have been updated. Manage Preferences Accept All Essential Only"
    },
    "https://jobs.snhu.edu/en/jobs/r0014714/student-residence-life-office-assistant/": {
      "title": "Student-Residence Life Office Assistant",
      "description": "Student-Residence Life Office Assistant,  | SNHU Careers Skip to main content Who We Are Who We Are Culture Benefits Equity, Diversity & Inclusion Military Career Areas Career Areas Online Teaching Jobs Academics & Teaching Business Operations & Technology Campus Staff Customer Service & Student Support Human Resources & Strategy Marketing & Communications Student Jobs Working at SNHU Working at SNHU Flexible Work Training & Development How We Hire 0 My Saved Jobs Search Jobs Student Jobs Student-Residence Life Office Assistant Part time September 12, 2026 On-Site (New Hampshire) Description Southern New Hampshire University is a team of innovators. World changers. Individuals who believe in progress with purpose. Since 1932, our people-centered strategy has defined us — and helped us grow a team that now serves over 180,000 learners worldwide. Our mission to transform lives is made possible by talented people who bring diverse industry experience, backgrounds and skills to the university. And today, we're ready to expand our reach. All we need is you. The opportunity Job Summary : Southern New Hampshire University is currently seeking a Student Worker as a Summer Front Desk Assistant for the Office of Residence life located in the Green Center on campus. Front Desk Assistants are students who work towards the accomplishment of the goals and objectives of the Office of Residence Life through providing support and assistance to central office members, prospective students, and current residents. This position’s primary focus is to ensure that the Office Residence Life has coverage and availability to assist and answer questions about housing. This position is open to any SNHU work study and commuter students are also welcome to apply. Essential Duties and Responsibilities: · Be present, attentive, and accessible to community members at the front desk in the Residence Life Office · Welcome community members into the office and direct them as needed, following central office assistant guidelines · Learning about Residence Life policies and processes · Attend Training session before scheduled shifts · Answer community members’ questions or direct them to offices/resources where they can find answers · Support Res Life staff with administrative tasks as assigned · Conduct basic organizational tasks in the office (work room, printer/office area, and desk itself) · Submit maintenance requests as needed · Help track and organize program supplies and equipment · Document any community members’ concerns that arise and share with supervisor · Connect with Residence Life staff or Public Safety as needed if any emergent, escalated, or disorderly situations occur · Enforce Residence Life policy · Support the guest registration process Minimum Qualifications: · Must be a full-time on campus student at Southern New Hampshire University · Policy violations will be reviewed and considered prior to position offers or pursuit of candidacy in the selection process . Students with Federal Work-Study may be prioritized Preferred Qualifications: · Applicants who have been an active member of a residential area for at least one semester before starting appointment Learning Outcomes: · Develop an understanding of community and the ways in which the front desk supports community development. · Demonstrate effective communication, organization, and problem-solving skills. We believe real innovation comes from inclusion - where different experiences, perspectives and talents are celebrated. So if you're wondering whether SNHU is right for you, take the leap and apply. You might be just the person we're looking for. If you have a disability and require a reasonable accommodation to fully engage in any part of the application or hiring process, please complete the Accommodation Request form or contact us at 603-626-9447. A member from the Employee Accommodation Support Center will be in contact with you within two business days to discuss your request. Compensation The hourly pay range for this position is $13.00 - $15.00. Actual offer will be based on skills, qualifications, experience and internal equity, in addition to relevant business considerations. Apply Now Save Saved Share Share Related Jobs Student ISS Office Assistant Save Saved Student Jobs On-Site (New Hampshire) Student - Make-A-Wish Office Assistant (Work-Study Only) Save Saved Student Jobs On-Site (New Hampshire) Student - UpReach Assistant to the Program Director (Work-Study Only) Save Saved Student Jobs On-Site (New Hampshire) See all jobs Expect the unexpected As a university, it’s no surprise we employ many talented academics. What you may not know is that SNHU isn’t solely made up of folks with higher ed experience. Not even close. Where will your talent take you? See all teams Academics & Teaching Business Operations & Technology Campus Staff Customer Service & Student Support Human Resources & Strategy Marketing & Communications Student Jobs Don't see the job you're looking for? Connect with us anyway! We post new jobs frequently, and joining our talent community is a great way to be notified when we do. Join talent community Sitemap Cookies Corporate site Need an Accommodation? © SNHU 2026, all rights reserved. Thank you, your preferences have been updated. Manage Preferences Accept All Essential Only"
    },
    "https://jobs.snhu.edu/en/jobs/r0014649/student-athletics-marketing-assistant/": {
      "title": "Student-Athletics Marketing Assistant",
      "description": "Student-Athletics Marketing Assistant,  | SNHU Careers Skip to main content Who We Are Who We Are Culture Benefits Equity, Diversity & Inclusion Military Career Areas Career Areas Online Teaching Jobs Academics & Teaching Business Operations & Technology Campus Staff Customer Service & Student Support Human Resources & Strategy Marketing & Communications Student Jobs Working at SNHU Working at SNHU Flexible Work Training & Development How We Hire 0 My Saved Jobs Search Jobs Student Jobs Student-Athletics Marketing Assistant Part time September 12, 2026 On-Site (New Hampshire) Description Southern New Hampshire University is a team of innovators. World changers. Individuals who believe in progress with purpose. Since 1932, our people-centered strategy has defined us — and helped us grow a team that now serves over 180,000 learners worldwide. Our mission to transform lives is made possible by talented people who bring diverse industry experience, backgrounds and skills to the university. And today, we're ready to expand our reach. All we need is you. The opportunity Job Summary Southern New Hampshire University is currently seeking a Student Worker as a Marketing Assistant for our Campus location to assist the Athletic Department with marketing needs. Job Responsibilities Assist the SNHU Associate AD and Marketing Coordinator in all aspects of daily operations. Creating promotional plans for a particular varsity sport(s). Organizing and implementing promotions, contests and other game day activities. Assisting with posting game day advertisements across campus weekly. Planning and executing special events for students, fans, and youth groups. Game day marketing management (including pre-game, in-game, post-game production). Coordination of events and game day activities, including item distribution, contests, information/field table set-up, and on-field presentations. Attend assigned home men and women's basketball and men's soccer games, as well as several hockey, women's soccer, baseball, field hockey, softball, track & field events as well as select playoff events. Brainstorming event ideas and creating plan of execution weekly. Minimum Qualifications Enrollment in an Undergraduate or Graduate Day program at SNHU. Work Study as part of their financial aid package. Preferred Qualifications: Photography experience Marketing experience Graphic Design experience Learning Outcomes (NACE Competencies): Become self-motivated independent worker Become versed in collegiate athletic marketing in all aspects Become a great teammate and work collaboratively Improve skills in graphic design, marketing, and promotional strategies Learn to communicate efficiently with a team during game day events Become a leader with connecting students in game day activities Work Schedule A combination of office hours during the week, working games on nights and weekends, and putting up signage early in the AM and taking down late in the evening. We believe real innovation comes from inclusion - where different experiences, perspectives and talents are celebrated. So if you're wondering whether SNHU is right for you, take the leap and apply. You might be just the person we're looking for. If you have a disability and require a reasonable accommodation to fully engage in any part of the application or hiring process, please complete the Accommodation Request form or contact us at 603-626-9447. A member from the Employee Accommodation Support Center will be in contact with you within two business days to discuss your request. Compensation The hourly pay range for this position is $13.00 - $15.00. Actual offer will be based on skills, qualifications, experience and internal equity, in addition to relevant business considerations. Apply Now Save Saved Share Share Related Jobs Student - Athletics Game Day and Equipment Supervisor Save Saved Student Jobs On-Site (New Hampshire) Student - Athletic Social Media Assistant Save Saved Student Jobs On-Site (New Hampshire) Student - Penmen Productions Broadcaster Save Saved Student Jobs On-Site (New Hampshire) See all jobs Expect the unexpected As a university, it’s no surprise we employ many talented academics. What you may not know is that SNHU isn’t solely made up of folks with higher ed experience. Not even close. Where will your talent take you? See all teams Academics & Teaching Business Operations & Technology Campus Staff Customer Service & Student Support Human Resources & Strategy Marketing & Communications Student Jobs Don't see the job you're looking for? Connect with us anyway! We post new jobs frequently, and joining our talent community is a great way to be notified when we do. Join talent community Sitemap Cookies Corporate site Need an Accommodation? © SNHU 2026, all rights reserved. Thank you, your preferences have been updated. Manage Preferences Accept All Essential Only"
